# passages/00002-FearoftheUnknownStart.mws.yaml
FearoftheUnknownStart_001=Fear of the Unknown
FearoftheUnknownStart_002=GENERATION I
FearoftheUnknownStart_003=**Letter from** **{randomname} -** _14 July, 1831._
FearoftheUnknownStart_004=It is with great reticence that I relay a grievous event which occurred upon my arrival. It is my hope that in penning these thoughts my mind will find solace from the foul images that have so firmly embedded themselves.
FearoftheUnknownStart_005=I will spare you the details of the journey to that dismal village to settle my deceased father's affairs. But upon entering its unpaved limits, my spouse drew my attention to several men and women galloping towards the town center, where there was a loud commotion and gathering of individuals. Intrigued by the local pageantry, I resolved to indulge my curiosity. I rapped my knuckles against the roof of the carriage and asked for the driver to turn towards the festivities.
FearoftheUnknownStart_006=He did not respond to my insistence. Nor did he respond when I thrice repeated my command. Frustrated, I angled my head out of the carriage window in order to speak more firmly. That is when I spied the horrific source of his obstinate and wise decision. For the briefest of moments — though a moment long enough for it to be etched within my memory forever — I saw the source of the commotion: A crowd of people surrounded a tall wooden stage where, swinging slowly from a thick hemp noose, hung a youthful woman. Her lifeless eyes stared in my direction before her form was obscured by buildings.
FearoftheUnknownStart_007=An irrational fear has gripped the populace. I swear it. The region is rife with superstitious traditions; traditions that do not mix well with the Church's rigid moral compass. When an individual from this close-knit community emerges from shuttered windows, they eye me as one would a foreigner, with sideways glances that make each excursion there insufferable. Accusations of witchcraft and voodooism erupt with increasing fervor, and paranoia weaves its tendrils into their minds.
FearoftheUnknownStart_008=Maybe this forced solitude will prove beneficial to my wits, as even amidst this clamor I find myself unnaturally focused. I have recently discovered my father's leather-bound journal and, while somewhat trite, I feel it has sparked something within me; a direction for my future studies, perhaps. Maybe it will offer some amusement in these trying times.
FearoftheUnknownStart_015=The {townname} {_rnd_FearoftheUnknownStart_0}

