# passages/00006-S4Kill1.mws.yaml
S4Kill1_001=A Public Execution?
S4Kill1_002=**{randomname}'s Journal -** _16 September, 1850. Romania._
S4Kill1_003=It is nearing midnight now, and I struggle to find my words. Is this remorse I feel, or elation? Even as I was swept into the midst of the frightened crowd, watching the flames swirl upwards, I was spellbound by their savagery. I could not imagine that this paranoia would be exercised so bluntly!
S4Kill1_004=It began over supper with my siblings: **The Blacksmith** - accused of practicing witchcraft - was carried past our brasserie to the steps of Town Hall. He wailed and protested his innocence, and when allowed use of his hands, he immediately accused Henriette, the town **Butcher**, of beguiling him. Within moments, he dramatically convulsed and acted as if under a trance when she decried his accusation.
S4Kill1_005=As we investigated the commotion that had interrupted our dessert course more closely, the **Blacksmith's** eyes blazed with fiery determination. He pled with us specifically. He would offer us his services, whatever we needed to spare his life.
S4Kill1_006=The **Butcher** was pressed to the steps of Town Hall. Silent, innocent as she approached, and forlorn. We knew that Henriette would offer the same deal.
S4Kill1_007=There was no way to slake the public's thirst for catharsis without bloodshed. Tonight, a witch was burned.

# passages/00007-S4Blacksmith.mws.yaml
S4Blacksmith_001=The Blacksmith is Dead.
S4Blacksmith_003=Though a ghastly event, it was perhaps fortunate. As the blaze extinguished and the crowd dispersed, no eyes cast their suspicious gaze upon myself, nor my cousins.
S4Blacksmith_004=Henriette was exceedingly appreciative of our vote of confidence and offered us a discount on her services. No questions asked.
S4Blacksmith_007=Each player who voted **NAY** quickly rummages through the Blacksmith's final offerings during the chaos and **gains 1** {icon:gears_icon}.

# passages/00008-S4Butcher.mws.yaml
S4Butcher_001=The Butcher is Dead.
S4Butcher_002=The Blacksmith laughed and shook each of our hands with a knowing wink. He will offer a deep discount on his services in the future. No questions asked.
S4Butcher_004=What an especially eventful dinner party. (Note to self - retrieve the recipe for the apricot glaze from tonight's menu.)
S4Butcher_005=Each player who voted **YAY** quickly rummages through the Butcher's stand during the chaos and **gains 1** {icon:animal_icon}.

# passages/00009-S4Witch1.mws.yaml
S4Witch1_001=Flames of Hysteria
S4Witch1_002=Paranoia Fades
S4Witch1_003=**Collected Letters -** _Stoker, Victoria - February 1863._
S4Witch1_005=With your return from university imminent, I thought it best to relay to you the state of affairs in {townname}.
S4Witch1_006=For a few years, I watched as the village's hostilities softened and the peasantry returned to their quaint ways of living. And as the years continued, the horrible spectacle of **the Blacksmith's execution** soon became a strictly taboo subject. Your scientific efforts and somewhat ignoble deeds were deemed eccentric. Each day, the townspeople grow more accepting of the exotic nature of the world.
S4Witch1_007=It is a curious thing to observe.
S4Witch1_010=For a few years, I watched as the village's hostilities softened and the peasantry returned to their quaint ways of living. But, before long, old rumors of pagan worship and occult manipulations resurfaced. The village has become united in the opinion that the **public execution of the humble Butcher** was a false spectacle, and that insidious characters still lurk within the town limits.
S4Witch1_011=Unfortunately, the town became further incensed and searched for an alternative solution.

# passages/00010-S4Witch2.mws.yaml
S4Witch2_001=More Secrets to Quell
S4Witch2_002=A Return to Civility
S4Witch2_003=**Collected Letters -** _Stoker, Victoria - February, 1863._
S4Witch2_004=You must forgive me for not responding sooner, but I must admit that there is not much to tell. While initially I suspected that the softening of the village's hostilities would be brief, indeed, old rumors of pagan worship and occult manipulations resurfaced in the coming years.
S4Witch2_005=However, these rumors were quelled by the boasts of townsfolk who had removed the evil blight on the land with torches and pitchforks. The **mob had been appeased** and the paranoia so entrenched within the village now appears a distant memory. 
S4Witch2_006=There is no need to rush home, though we send you warm wishes all the same.
S4Witch2_007=You must forgive the lateness of my writing, but as your caretaker, I regret to say that I am not very acquainted with the quill. I have kept your affairs in order to the best of my ability, but I am troubled by recent events in {townname}.
S4Witch2_008=For a few years, I watched as the village's hostilities softened and the peasantry returned to their quaint ways of living. But, before long, old rumors of pagan worship and occult manipulations resurfaced.
S4Witch2_009=With **no one overtaken to slake the mob's thirst**, their intense fear of outsiders has surged into a frenzy.
S4Witch2_010=I fear their suspicions have increased. Please be safe in your return.

