S4Foreign1_010=**{wal}**
S4Foreign1_011= or more bricks in total have been collected, 
S4Foreign1_012=click here to build the Memorial Wall.
S4Foreign1_013=Otherwise, 
S4Foreign1_014=click here to build a proper Memorial.

# passages/00016-S4Jail2.mws.yaml
S4Jail2_001=Money Talks
S4Jail2_005=Since your last letter, I have heard rumors that with **generous financial backing** from some anonymous donors, they are expanding the Asylum. Given your disposition, I would not be surprised to discover that you had a direct hand in it.
S4Jail2_006=I say it is a positive thing, this mental rehabilitation. I've always been intrigued by the potential of the human mind both to adapt and to be adapted upon. Though, I suggest you keep your distance. They may mistake your jocularity for insanity and admit you. Wouldn't that be something?
S4Jail2_008=Is it true they have plans to convert the Asylum into a private penitentiary? If I were to venture a guess, I would assume **your investments** may have had a hand in it.
S4Jail2_009=Well, I say good riddance. The thought of spending precious resources to reform a mind already lost when they could be put to better use manually. It is like trying to unrotten a rotten fruit!

# passages/00017-IsolationIntro.mws.yaml
IsolationIntro_001=Isolation and Ignorance
IsolationIntro_003=**Letter from** **{randomname} -** _30 March, 1892. Romania._
IsolationIntro_004=I tell you, these damn peasants actually built a wall around their own town. In the 1800's no less! These fools have traded paranoia for utter delusion!
IsolationIntro_005=Do they expect a foreign government to set up a military line and trebuchets to lay siege to this backwater stronghold? What on earth would it offer them? Trade has suffered. Prices have risen. And most importantly, with the caravans left to go elsewhere, I must find alternative ways to procure knowledge.
IsolationIntro_006=Why just this week, I was enraged by the audacity of the intrusion into my affairs! I, the rightful heir to a considerable estate, was forced to suffer the indignity of a physical inspection at what appeared to be a freshly fashioned gateway to the village where I was born. And then, to infer that I was bound by duty to prove my citizenship? My spouse was so manhandled that they were forced to spend the next week in their bedroom consumed by anxious thoughts.
IsolationIntro_007=Curse this infernal world filled with frustrations and complications at every turn! If only these regressive tendencies toward isolationism could have been resolved in another way! Surely, you can determine how dire the situation has become if it has rattled my notoriously pragmatic disposition. How can one change the world when it so decidedly wants to remain the same?
IsolationIntro_008=Mark my words, I would sooner watch these ramparts crumble than allow them to destroy my spirit. I will find a way to circumvent this oppressive state and preserve my legacy at all costs!

# passages/00018-TensionIntro.mws.yaml
TensionIntro_001=Old Habits
TensionIntro_002=**Journal of** **{randomname} -** _April 1892._
TensionIntro_003=Ah, what relief it is for one to not spend each waking moment fearing they will be burned at the stake! The oppressive hostilities of the Romanian countryside, of which I had become familiar during my youth, made the anxiety of my carriage-bound return to the old estate a dreadful prospect.
TensionIntro_004=Yet, even as the ink dried upon the executor's paperwork, my spouse and I quietly enjoyed our coffee against the bustle of a cobblestone street. The only eyes upon us were those clearly impressed by our bright, Parisian attire. Never once did an errant gaze suggest I would be shot with a revolver or murdered viciously by a stiletto. It was almost disappointing.
TensionIntro_005=With the town's decision to forgo construction of a barrier, the emergence of additional trade and the ceasing of xenophobic hostilities has allowed further interaction with other cultures. I find myself entertaining exotic guests that pique my darker interests. The occult and its superstitious effects on my family's past has become a peculiar fascination. Spiritualism being the fashion these days, you know.
TensionIntro_006=However, "old habits die hard" as the saying goes, and a delicious tension roils beneath the surface of the town. Acceptance (or apathy) may have calmed the tempest of hatred, but I realize that this deep psychological infection has yet to be fully reconciled. With each visit, I feel my actions push these factions closer until they will be forced to make a potentially devastating and amusing decision.
TensionIntro_007=It is an experiment in itself; a powder keg waiting to go off. And I am desperate to observe the results.

# passages/00019-Isolation.mws.yaml
Isolation_002=Turn to page **14** of the Village Chronicle. Place the Suspicion Marker on space **{tracker}** and the {icon:angrymob_icon} token one space to the left. Return all Memorial bricks to the Scenario box.
Isolation_003=**Rising Prices**
Isolation_004=With the town's isolation in full force, the cost of business has increased. Any space with a **$1 payment** symbol requires the player to **pay $1** to take the action listed.

