# passages/00021-S4Asylum.mws.yaml
S4Asylum_002=The Asylum, while marginally effective in its treatments, appears to be struggling financially - something which I had cautioned earlier about the town's philanthropic pursuits. Lock a deranged person in a room and inevitably the cost of care will outweigh the revenue received.
S4Asylum_003=Of course, I was once again asked for assistance: "Surely you are familiar with Hanwell Asylum and the recent progressive reforms presented by Mattineau. Rehabilitation is the moral treatment option,” they repeated. I was glad that at least in this scenario, their fundraising efforts came with a tangible reward.
S4Asylum_004=Retrieve the **{asylumup}** Estate Upgrades from the Scenario box.

# passages/00022-S4Creature1.mws.yaml
S4Creature1_001=Grandfather's Creation Returns
S4Creature1_002=The lumbering Creature has returned to claim its request. If we are unable to provide, the consequences will be severe.
S4Creature1_003=**Did we create the {did1} that the creature requested?**
S4Creature1_004=If we **created the {did1}** as requested, 
S4Creature1_005=If we did **NOT**, 

# passages/00023-PrivatizedIntro.mws.yaml
PrivatizedIntro_001=Conducting Business
PrivatizedIntro_003=I will keep this letter brief — as brief as I can. You are aware that brevity is not my strongest suit. However, it is August, the ink struggles to dry in the humidity, and my mind is set on complicated things. Perhaps it would be more amiable to pen this missive in my own blood, cold as I am perceived to be by the inhabitants of this gray, lifeless city. It would certainly bring a little more color to it.
PrivatizedIntro_004=You are probably interested in matters of business, and it is going exceedingly well, or so I hear — I struggle to keep the figures in my head. I, and regrettably my good cousins, whom I love dearly, have invested directly in the town's well-being and now own a substantial portion of the commercial district. It appears that my parent's investments have paid off handsomely.
PrivatizedIntro_005=News of the day: The Asylum Project, which I believe was misguided from the beginning, has become a more intriguing source of labor. It's not that I believe that rehabilitation of the deviant mindset is impossible, it simply requires a more aggressive therapy than they were willing to indulge. With our unmediated assistance and the endorsement of the state, a prison is a more versatile testing ground.
PrivatizedIntro_006=And I — I am doing well. It disconcerts me. My studies continue with great passion that consumes me more than anything I have ever known. Even the dismal fog that looms across this bleak valley fills me with a solemn peace. Yet it is that same calm which causes my unease.
PrivatizedIntro_007=I must work quickly, as I feel something unseen watches, waiting to emerge from the shadows. I cannot have destiny torn from my grasp just when I reach the pinnacle!
PrivatizedIntro_009=The Bloodsmith
PrivatizedIntro_011=Lose 5VP
PrivatizedIntro_012=Discard a Vanity Estate Upgrade from your Estate if possible.

# passages/00024-LiberalIntro.mws.yaml
LiberalIntro_002=I apologize for the tardiness of my reply, but settling the matters of my inheritance has uncovered distressing revelations that haunt my waking hours. It is terrible. And by terrible, I mean decent, cheerful, and painfully dull. People stroll around this inviting town, greet each other with smiles, and share baked goods. Baked goods! How are they so blind to the dark realities of the world? How did we arrive at such an excruciatingly positive conclusion?
LiberalIntro_003=While other institutions across Europe experienced the ravenous strain of overcrowding, our town’s well-funded lunatic asylum proved a luminous model of rehabilitation. Restraints were traded for personal care from the staff and a work release program was expanded for patients eager to assimilate themselves into society once again, with the skills to succeed.
LiberalIntro_004=It is an interesting concept in theory, but one which we know will only end in folly. When I made a brief visit to the Asylum Program (as they now so boldly call it), they even attempted to evaluate me as if I had been admitted. Apparently, the country has turned to more civilized ways to disenfranchise individuals that they fear — not to mention the additional taxes levied against legitimate entrepreneurs such as myself.
LiberalIntro_005=Like mighty Atlas, I will accept these heavy charges. While I disagree with their methodology, and the expenses of this progressive approach will certainly be a financial burden, access to skilled labor does appeal to me from an efficiency standpoint, if they have the stomach for it.
LiberalIntro_006=The days are certainly bright here in the valley, but in the end, this light will only make my family's work shine more brilliantly!

# passages/00025-Privatized.mws.yaml
Privatized_002=Shuffle them and randomly place one token on each Location shown on the Village Chronicle without looking at the opposite side. Keep any remaining tokens in a supply nearby.
Privatized_003=**Investment in Town**
Privatized_004=To visit a Location with a {icon:s2_coloredmoneytoken} token in another player's color, you must **pay $1** to the owner of the token. _($1 total for each visit even if multiple pieces are placed at the same time.)_
Privatized_005=**Jail**
Privatized_006=Our business investments have created new opportunities. When you visit the Jail, you may **pay $1** to take a Perform Experiment action.
Privatized_009=At the end of each round, an expedition sets off to kill the Creature. All players on a successful expedition receive **5VP.**For a detailed explanation of the hunt, 

# passages/00026-Liberal.mws.yaml
Liberal_001=Turn to page **10** of the Village Chronicle.
Liberal_002=Turn to page **11** of the Village Chronicle.
Liberal_003=Shuffle them and randomly place one token onto each Location shown on the Village Chronicle without looking at the opposite side. Keep any remaining tokens in a supply nearby.

# passages/00027-S4Jail1.mws.yaml
S4Jail1_001=The Creature's Aid
S4Jail1_003=Your previous letter appeared rushed and ended with incoherent scribblings. What is this creature business and why have you failed "in the eyes of god" by **aiding the poor thing**? Are you quite sure about your own mental state? 
S4Jail1_004=I have heard a rumor that the **Asylum has expanded**. Perhaps your recent bout of good will spawned this charitable fortune. Whether it is so or not, my friend, I would refer you to it. Not necessarily by way of admitting yourself - unless you feel obliged - but perhaps they could recommend you a remedy to calm your thoughts. I suspect you may require more than a spot of tea and bed rest.
S4Jail1_005=What is this nonsense I hear about a hideous **creature left stalking about the countryside** in your region? I ask you only because your recent letters about experiments have been quite unforthcoming.
S4Jail1_006=I may disagree with your methods, but I have always attempted to stand by you as an academic. Allowing a monster to wander through the land unchecked, and by many accounts stealing and murdering along the way; why I believe this is sufficient grounds for which to end a friendship.
S4Jail1_007=This decision has caused people to **lose faith in the security of the Asylum**, thinking now that madmen are running through the streets. And I certainly don't blame them.

# passages/00028-S4GoodCreature.mws.yaml
S4GoodCreature_001=The Creature is Appeased
S4GoodCreature_002=I have made peace with the monster, though in so doing I have ensured my place in the fires of hell. With my death, I free my heir from the shackles of sin. My sacrifice will not be in vain! The legacy will transcend me.
S4GoodCreature_003=So ends the curse upon my family.

# passages/00029-S4BadCreature.mws.yaml
S4BadCreature_001=The Creature Exacts Its Revenge
S4BadCreature_002=I am ruined! Oh how naive I had been to ignore the warnings of my mother and father. They warned me to be vigilant! But I was too proud to believe in superstitious and illogical things such as curses!
S4BadCreature_003=As I slept last night, my estate was breached by a stealthy and merciless beast! And when I awoke, it was to an empty bed and the sound of screaming. I rushed to the window only to see the Creature with his disfigured face carved into a sinister grin, his hands and clothes stained red. He held a burning torch aloft while his black stallion reared. With a swift pull on the reins, he escaped deep into the forest.
S4BadCreature_004=Hours later, the pall only darkened as news of my cousins' own tragedies weepingly arrived. A similar fate had befallen their spouses as they were wrenched from the living world by the beast.
S4BadCreature_005=I have only sorrow and hatred left roiling in my heart! I vow to remove that cursed thing from the Earth and reclaim my family's legacy!
S4BadCreature_006=All players place their **Spouse** piece into the **game box**. _This piece cannot be used for the remainder of the game._
S4BadCreature_007=All players gain a {icon:bodies_icon} from the supply.

# passages/00030-S4Smug.mws.yaml
S4Smug_001=Barely Legal Importation
S4Smug_002=I am unsure as to how to proceed. Tonight, I received a smarmy gentlewoman for dinner who introduced herself as the new proprietor of a local warehouse. The purpose of her visit was immediately clear and especially brazen. There was only one reason why anyone would invest in a declining town such as {townname} and her resultant smirk was confirmation: illicit trade.
S4Smug_003=The smuggling business is booming as the town's relations with the country deteriorate, this I know. The immediate benefits are enticing, however with any agreement that stretches the law, **there may be consequences.** I'm sure it is nothing life-threatening, but still, is it a gamble worth taking?
S4Smug_004=**Accepting the Offer**
S4Smug_005=Once per round, each player may visit the **Smuggler's Dock** Location in Town. Upon visiting, **gain 2 Ingredients of your choice**. Then, click the Storybook to determine the consequences of your indiscretion.
S4Smug_006=Turn to page **15** in the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00031-S4Con1.mws.yaml
S4Con1_001=Caught in the Act
S4Con1_003=These charlatans have sentenced me without trial. They say they have evidence of my 'obviously smuggling a large amount of exotic product on the roof of my carriage,' but of course they are unwilling to present it to me or my legal representation.
S4Con1_004=I have, due to the pressures of angry villagers who call for vigilante justice, decided against pursuing the slanderous issue as they have not pressed charges. Their faces tell me all that I need to know about how I will be hounded by this public assassination of character.
S4Con1_005=**Gain 2 {icon:creepy_icon}.**

# passages/00032-S4Con2.mws.yaml
S4Con2_001=The Trial
S4Con2_002=I have been served a notice to appear at the courthouse next week. Can you imagine? The police refuse to present evidence until the trial begins. Of course, my lawyer is the best that money can buy, but these heathens may create farcical evidence that is substantially damning. I am not sure it is worth the risk.
S4Con2_004=You may pay **${_rnd_S4Con2_0}** to guarantee the success of your case, OR accept the outcome of the trial (which has a 1/3 chance of succeeding).
S4Con2_005=Pay the $ to the supply and click here.
S4Con2_006=Accept the Outcome.

# passages/00033-S4Con3.mws.yaml
S4Con3_001=Politics as Usual
S4Con3_002=I will not carry on this farce any longer. I admit that I smuggled goods from the docks. This I would do again, I swear, as it is an affront to my sensibilities that I should be so deprived of the resources which I require just to appease these peons.
S4Con3_003=It does not matter. The public is too focused on recent events and it is an act that everyone has engaged in. I suspect there will be little to no repercussions.
S4Con3_004=Gain 1 {icon:creepy_icon} for being weird.

# passages/00034-ThistenseBad.mws.yaml
ThistenseBad_001=Come to an Agreement
ThistenseBad_002=**Journal of {randomname} -** _25 June, 1901._
ThistenseBad_003=When the tensions heightened to their breaking point and bloodshed was just moments away, they came to a startling epiphany. They finally realized that they have one thing truly in common.
ThistenseBad_004=They hate **us.**
ThistenseBad_005=Remove the **Romani token** {icon:s2_romanitoken} from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.

# passages/00035-S4IsoBrick.mws.yaml
S4IsoBrick_001=Most Honored Philanthropist
S4IsoBrick_002=The mayor of the town, in a brief ceremony on the steps of the Town Hall, offered the most important individual in the construction of the memorial a solid gold **Key to the City** today.
S4IsoBrick_003=The player who collected the most **Brick** tokens gains a **Key to the City** Estate Upgrade. That player also gains **{_rnd_S4IsoBrick_0}VP**. _Ties are broken by the one with the fewest VP. If still tied, the one who went last this round._
S4IsoBrick_004=The player who collected the second-most **brick** tokens simply gains a **Key to the City** Estate Upgrade.
S4IsoBrick_005=_Note: Do not discard the brick tokens until instructed._

