# passages/00049-Expedition1.mws.yaml
Expedition1_002=Expedition 3:
Expedition1_003=Expedition 1:
Expedition1_004=Expedition 2:
Expedition1_005=The snow-covered landscape and bitter cold made following the trail of the Creature a difficult and time-consuming endeavor.
Expedition1_006=It took months of preparation, but even as I set out upon this blasted hunt to seek revenge against the abomination, I was not quite sure which way to venture.
Expedition1_007=A hard journey lay ahead. While my body was weary from the excursion, the hatred in my heart fueled me as I awoke each morning searching for any sign of the Creature's activities.
Expedition1_008= {_rnd_Expedition1_0} However, from the clues I was able to uncover from those I spoke with in the town, I knew that there was a chance. With luck, I would be able to destroy the beast once and for all.

# passages/00051-Liberal3.mws.yaml
Liberal3_001=**RehabilitationToken**
Liberal3_002=At the end of each round, an expedition sets off to kill the Creature. All players on a successful expedition receive **5VP.** For a detailed explanation of the Hunt, 
Liberal3_003=Click here at the end of the round to commence the expedition.

# passages/00052-ExpYes.mws.yaml
ExpYes_001=The Creature is Killed
ExpYes_002=**Journal of** _name illegible_
ExpYes_003=Success. Oh, if words could adequately describe the crestfallen look on the monstrosity's distorted face as it realized its life was at an end! My servants and I subdued the foul Creature, binding it with rope around its wrists and legs and suspending it upon a felled birch tree with little struggle.
ExpYes_004=Kindled with underbrush and pine needles, I watched as the smoke turned to flame and slowly consumed the monster. First, the frostbitten feet and legs clad in tattered cloth, then the rusted belt-buckle searing through flesh as it fell red-hot into the fire.
ExpYes_005=It did not scream as it expired, nor did it writhe in agony, as if the pain of its own existence had already overwhelmed all possible sensation. It merely stared in my direction with a forlorn look in its eyes, like all the world had foresaken it. I could not bear the sight. I raised my pistol and shot it dead.
ExpYes_006=Each player on the successful expedition receives **5VP.**
ExpYes_007=Collect and return all Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront} to the Scenario box.

# passages/00053-ExpNo.mws.yaml
ExpNo_001=The Creature Escapes
ExpNo_002=**Journal of** _name illegible_ **-** _(cont.)_
ExpNo_003=I saw the silhouette of the Creature set against the paleness of the moon. Its hideous features squelched and seethed beneath torn clothing as it bellowed out to the valley before disappearing once again into the mists.
ExpNo_004=I reached for my pistol, but found myself abruptly shaken as the image dissipated and I awoke upon my bedroll under the dawn's light. Though my nightmares had grown more vivid with each passing evening, the voyage returned no sign of the Creature. Days hence, I was forced to return empty-handed.
ExpNo_005=Collect all Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront}from all players. Turn them all so the yellow crosshairs are face-up.
ExpNo_006=Shuffle them and randomly place one token on each Location shown on the Village Chronicle without looking at the opposite side. Keep any remaining tokens in a supply nearby. There will be another expedition at the end of this round.
ExpNo_007=Collect and return all Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront}to the Scenario box.

# passages/00054-LiberalEvent.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent_001=Economic Stimulus
LiberalEvent_002=As I predicted, the Romanian government's expanding social programs have left it unmercifully poor during this brief recession. I have made protective strides to divert my portfolio abroad, so the impact has been negligible. However, the upheaval caused by this Great War has sparked nationalist sentiments and minor rebellions across Transylvania.
LiberalEvent_003=The sudden mantra to protect our own has devolved into a battle within the government. I yawn when I dwell on parliamentary matters for too long. I'm sure it is some endless babble about race, human rights, and religious faith.
LiberalEvent_004=The result of this prejudice is that now Transylvania is faced with a dreary decision that has no positive outcome. As landowners and entrepreneurs, naturally, we will make this decision as to how the regional government will proceed.

# passages/00055-StoryBook.mws.yaml
StoryBook_001=How to Use the Storybook
StoryBook_002=My Father's Work is a game of Victorian era mad scientist ambition told over three Generations. The Storybook App controls the direction of the Town depending on the decisions made by players. It will require that players interact with it by clicking on specific passages at certain times.
StoryBook_003=**End of Round**
StoryBook_004=There are three rounds in each Generation. At the end of each round, you **must** click the bottom link to resolve any special events and move play to the next round. The screen will then display the current round and changes to gameplay (if any).
StoryBook_005=**Story Actions**
StoryBook_006=Sometimes the game will require that a player click a certain link when an action has been performed. This may be taking an action in the Town, your Estate, or completing a specific goal. Be sure to click these links to receive a special story passage.

