# passages/00070-Witchwolfresolution.mws.yaml
Witchwolfresolution_001=Accusations
Witchwolfresolution_002=Word travels quickly in these parts. For as distant I am from the civilized world, I am equidistant from any meaningful activity to gossip about. While I'm sure you have heard of the recent family tragedy, I wanted you to read it from my own words.
Witchwolfresolution_003=As cousins, we frequently sup together when time and weather allows. But woefully, one occasion we chose a night where the wind howled remorselessly and set the locust trees to rapping against the estate windows. Upon this uneasy evening, we spied a great light beaming from the forest, and soon a throng of townspeople rallied around the exterior walls, waving torches and brandishing pitchforks.
Witchwolfresolution_004=The townspeople blamed us for bringing a blight of witchcraft upon their town. Tonight, they demanded a sacrifice and no amount of persuasion would slake their thirst for blood. As the hounds kept them at bay, we were forced to make a sanguine decision that would haunt us for the remainder of our days.

# passages/00071-WallEvent.mws.yaml
WallEvent_001=Memorial to the Past for the Future
WallEvent_002=As expected - and as I've relayed to you so amusingly in the past - the town is not seeing adequate support for their memorial. This time, however, I was distinctly unamused to have my experimentations interrupted just as I had secured a moment's peace. Only yesterday, well-dressed representatives from the local government (mind you, as well-dressed as a fop with a decade's old sense of fashion can be) visited the estate in person to ask for my assistance.
WallEvent_003=When I pressed as to the actual purpose of our donations, they act as a parakeet with its cage door rattled; wildly gesticulating and talking vaguely about eliminating all possible superstition and influence from the town to make it prosperous again. Quite unlikely, I would say.
WallEvent_004=My dealings with the local Romani merchants have made it clear that whatever the town's petty inclinations, the memorial will have a deep affect on their trade. The Romani do not wish to leave the region, but will do so if pressed.

# passages/00072-Witchres1.mws.yaml
Witchres1_001=Death and Resolution
Witchres1_002=Each player with a finger pointed at **{witch} gains 3VP**. All other players receive nothing.
Witchres1_003=The {wsuspect} points at **{pointAI}**!
Witchres1_004=They claim to have seen their foul sneers from the darkness, orchestrating this entire farce!
Witchres1_005=They state that they hope now that their hideous secrets will come to light!
Witchres1_006={_rnd_Witchres1_0} Include this accusation when tabulating the number of fingers pointed at a player.
Witchres1_007=Click on the player below with the most fingers pointed at them _(if there is a tie, the one with the most VP among the tied players. If there is still a tie, the earlier player in turn order in the previous round.)_:

