CheckWitches1_010=**{nameE} hexing the {witE}**

# passages/00074-Witchres2.mws.yaml
Witchres2_001=Cursed Removal
Witchres2_003=The town was appeased by our decision to forgo familial obligations and offer one of our own as a necessary sacrifice. I do not know how to state it other than with sober words. To lose a family member, oh it is a torment to my very soul.
Witchres2_004=I only wish they would have taken it better. Poor, {witch}, spat at us and made a frightfully unbecoming scene while being burnt at the stake.
Witchres2_005=It was I who was chosen. Harboring no ill will towards my cousins, I bravely faced death and was granted a minor reprieve by the mob to attend to my final affairs, which is how I am able to pen this missive to you in my final days. The stories to the contrary that describe me weeping hysterically and begging are pure fabrication.
Witchres2_006=I would never harm anyone and I would never use this peculiar circumstance to further complicate affairs for my cousins.
Witchres2_007=The town was appeased by our wise decision to sacrifice the true culprit in this macabre, mystical mystery. Let it be known that seeking vengeance can carry with it a terrible and fatal cost.
Witchres2_008=I only wish the wretch would have taken it better when they were found out. Poor, {witch}, spat at us and made a frightfully unbecoming scene while being burnt at the stake. Ghastly manners.
Witchres2_009=**{witch}** must place their Self token into Lost. This piece cannot be retrieved for the remainder of this Generation.
Witchres2_010=Then, {witch} places the Witch's Hex {icon:s2_witchhextoken} token on the Location of their choice. _This cannot be the Church._
Witchres2_011=The vile {wsuspect} performs one last bit of witchcraft before expiring in the flames.
Witchres2_012=Place the Witch's Hex {icon:s2_witchhextoken} token on the **{hexAI}.**

# passages/00075-Witchres3.mws.yaml
Witchres3_001=The Curse Continues
Witchres3_002=The town was appeased by our decision to forgo familial obligations and offer one of our own as a necessary sacrifice. And it was indeed a necessary action as this individual had become too grandiose, too conspicuous in their actions. How could we be blamed? I cannot be scrutinized, suspected dubiously at every turn! It was the only logical course.
Witchres3_003=However, in the ensuing months, it become apparent that our sacrifice only obscured the real truth. {falsewitch} was not the cursed one. And perhaps none of us truly were.
Witchres3_004=It was I who was chosen! I barely escaped that evening with my life and this letter is penned to you swiftly from my estate whilst I await judgement.
Witchres3_005=They knew! They knew I was not some cursed being! Does their jealousy know no bounds? They conspired against me - to force me into exile, unable to perform my most important tasks! A pox on them! My legacy will live on and it will emerge stronger!
Witchres3_006=Death is only the beginning!
Witchres3_007=I can state with clear conscious that while the members of my family chose an innocent individual as the inevitable target of the mob's ire, it was certainly not our intention for them to receive such a swift and fiery punishment. Burning a witch at the stake - in the 1800's? Why, the thought that I instead could have been the recipient of such barbarism causes me intestinal discomfort.
Witchres3_008=**{falsewitch}** may **perform one Estate action** immediately without placing a piece.
Witchres3_009=**{falsewitch}** must then place their Self piece into Lost. This piece cannot be retrieved until the End of this Generation.
Witchres3_010=The innocent {wsuspect} curses us with their dying breath. Their pleas are enough to make the townsfolk suspicious.
Witchres3_011=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} marker one space to the left.

# passages/00076-HuntExplanation.mws.yaml
HuntExplanation_001=At the end of each round, an expedition sets off to kill the Creature. This expedition is led by the player(s) who has collected the most Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront}. _The Storybook will prompt you to compare totals. All tied players go on the expedition together. You may secretly look at your Hunt tokens_ {icon:s2_hunttokenfront} _when you collect them._
HuntExplanation_002=The player(s) leading the expedition reveals their tokens and counts up the total number of **Clues** {icon:s2_hunttokenbackred} on the reverse side. If you have collected a number of **Clues** {icon:s2_hunttokenbackred} equal or greater than the expedition amount needed: the expedition succeeds and the Creature is killed.
HuntExplanation_003=All players on a successful expedition receive **5VP.**
HuntExplanation_004=If unsuccessful, another expedition will begin at the end of the next round.

# passages/00077-PrivateNOTES.mws.yaml
PrivateNOTES_001=DELETE MANHUNT STUFF
PrivateNOTES_003=Minor consequence
PrivateNOTES_004=What does the {warden} want?
PrivateNOTES_005=- vindication
PrivateNOTES_006=- revenge on you - will only spare one
PrivateNOTES_007=- the best creation to win in the battledome
PrivateNOTES_008=What does the Creature do?
PrivateNOTES_009=- Bad
PrivateNOTES_010=- Good (Event gives what bonus?)
PrivateNOTES_011=What does visiting the {warden} do?
PrivateNOTES_012=- bring a tribute, do something useful
PrivateNOTES_013=What do you get for impressing the warden?
PrivateNOTES_014=- you are truly not like your ancestors
PrivateNOTES_015=Obsession Cards unlock positive or negative.
PrivateNOTES_016=SHOW UP - Business as usual. Act like the original setup with tokens.
PrivateNOTES_017=End of 1st Gen
PrivateNOTES_018=Race to the end of the Creepy Track for a bonus.
PrivateNOTES_019=Rules for later
PrivateNOTES_020=Servants cannot enter TOWN until you have reached or exceeded the Angry Mob Marker.
PrivateNOTES_021=Caretaker pieces can enter TOWN.

# passages/00078-CheckWitches2.mws.yaml
CheckWitches2_001=**{wsuspect} hexing the {witAI2}**
CheckWitches2_002=**{nameA} hexing the {witA2}**
CheckWitches2_003=**{nameB} hexing the {witB2}**
CheckWitches2_004=**{nameC} hexing the {witC2}**
CheckWitches2_005=**{nameD} hexing the {witD2}**
CheckWitches2_006=**{nameE} hexing the {witE2}**

# passages/00079-CheckW1.mws.yaml
CheckW1_014=**Newsprint - {newspaper} -** _{_rnd_CheckW1_0} {_rnd_CheckW1_1}, 1_
CheckW1_015=_{_rnd_CheckW1_3}_
CheckW1_016=_{_rnd_CheckW1_2}_
CheckW1_017=Hauntings continue to be reported near the {witch1} in town. While opinions differ as to the strength of the spiritual presence or the source of the paranormal events, one aspect is readily agreed upon: a curse is upon the town! And we here at the {newspaper} have verified sources which confirm these suspicious activities.

# passages/00080-CheckW2.mws.yaml
CheckW2_001=**Newsprint - {newspaper} -** _{_rnd_CheckW2_0} {_rnd_CheckW2_1}, 1_
CheckW2_002=_{_rnd_CheckW2_3}_
CheckW2_003=_{_rnd_CheckW2_2}_
CheckW2_004=gentleman
CheckW2_005=gentlewoman
CheckW2_006=Yesterday morning, a {_rnd_CheckW2_4} was assisted in the streets outside {witch2}. After a sudden collapse, observers attest to the body beginning to writhe with reflexive muscle motions. As passersby rushed to their immediate aid, they were ushered to a nearby home, where the convulsions began to dissipate.
CheckW2_007=Our representatives have obtained sensitive information from those close to the proceedings, and their accounts indicate foul play.

# passages/00081-S4Foreign3.mws.yaml
S4Foreign3_001=Protected Against Witchcraft
S4Foreign3_002=The movement to protect our fair village from the outsider's influence has succeeded. Today, the construction of the Memorial Wall had its ground-breaking ceremony at the site of the new Town Gate. The Wall is planned to run over three thousand meters, encircling the entirety of {townname} in a thick barrier of stone and iron.
S4Foreign3_003=**The witch is still out there.** It is our hope at {newspaper} that this wall will keep out all unwanted, foreign influences and protect the righteous citizens from the evils just outside our doors. {townname}! {townname}!
S4Foreign3_004=Several years have passed since the **fatal accusation of {witch}** for the crime of witchcraft. Since that unfortunate, yet necessary, event, no further reports of dark spirits have emerged. With aristocratic eccentricities blamed as the predominant cause of this paranoia, {townname}'s mayor has spearheaded efforts to rebuild its tainted reputation.
S4Foreign3_005=In a direct display of this newfound resolve, plans for the Memorial Wall, a project proposed over a decade ago, have been officially canceled per the mayor's speech earlier today. In its place, a new Memorial building project is scheduled for construction later this year. The new Memorial stands as both a celebration of diversity and a reminder of the dark years that {townname} endured. As such, it has sparked renewed controversy.

# passages/00082-WitchIntro.mws.yaml
WitchIntro_001=The Deadly Witching Game
WitchIntro_002=**{randomname}'s Journal -** _2 December, 1862._
WitchIntro_003=The townsfolk grow agitated by my presence, claiming that my family carries a curse and only tragedy befalls those who align themselves with us over the years. After the untimely death of several of my cousins' mutual business partners, and the appearance of blood pentagrams at various locations within town, even I began to find it suspicious. Was it a supernatural manifestation – a dark power willed to one of us – or mere happenstance?
WitchIntro_004=We also could not overlook the possibility of the {wsuspect} perhaps enacting a misguided sort of vengeance with the entire affair. I had noticed them skulking about during my early visits to town and the events of decades past clearly weighed heavily upon them.
WitchIntro_005=While the townspeople squabbled over superstition, we, intellectuals, decided to put the scientific method to good use in order to determine which of us had become cursed.

# passages/00083-Mobbed2.mws.yaml
Mobbed2_001=Fear of Our Family
Mobbed2_002=**{randomname}'s Journal -** _June 1862._
Mobbed2_003=The deep-rooted effects of mass paranoia are difficult for even time to assuage. Though I have suffered greatly due to cruel ignorance of these fools, I am well aware that my children will also know it well. These unfounded suspicions would surely haunt us from generation to generation.
Mobbed2_004=Click here to determine the Fate of the Town.
Mobbed2_005={nameA} gains a **Family Plot** Estate Upgrade and must add it to their Estate immediately.
Mobbed2_006={nameB} gains a **Family Plot** Estate Upgrade and must add it to their Estate immediately.
Mobbed2_007={nameC} gains a **Family Plot** Estate Upgrade and must add it to their Estate immediately.
Mobbed2_008={nameD} gains a **Family Plot** Estate Upgrade and must add it to their Estate immediately.
Mobbed2_009={nameE} gains a **Family Plot** Estate Upgrade and must add it to their Estate immediately.

# passages/00084-ConsequencesTense.mws.yaml
ConsequencesTense_001=Comeuppance
ConsequencesTense_002=They were supposed to rip one another to shreds! There was no other possible outcome! A spirited town meeting was scheduled for today and the tension surely was a powder keg mere moments from erupting. Instead, I waited upon my veranda, watching the city seethe in the valley below until my tea grew cold.
ConsequencesTense_003=The news came by courier several hours later. From the notes provided, it appears that one constant had plagued the town of {townname} for the entirety of its existence. Us. Our family's choices through the generations have had a decisive impact on the history of tensions within the town.
ConsequencesTense_004=They were thorough in their assessment. 
ConsequencesTense_005=While frontier justice in the town's history is certainly a negative, our grandparents' choice to hang the **guilty party** still resonated.
ConsequencesTense_006=The town's dark history and our grandparents' choice to support the senseless killing of an obviously **innocent individual** is noted.
ConsequencesTense_007=Successfully **unmasking the cursed individual** was seen as a notable element of moral character.
ConsequencesTense_008=Our parents' **inability to determine who the cursed witch was** weighed heavily on their minds.
ConsequencesTense_009=The Romani remember that we chose to **support Acceptance** and only offered meager support for the town's misguided endeavors.
ConsequencesTense_010=The Romani remember our misguided decision to **provide Strength** to the town.
ConsequencesTense_011=The town weighed these options and quickly came to an agreement.

# passages/00085-LiberalEvent2.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent2_001=Surprising Rebuke
LiberalEvent2_002=Outrageous! Our representative in parliament returns our correspondence with a sharp rebuke of our attempts to use our influence to alter the purely democratic process. Would they really leave this matter to popular opinion? This ignoble disrespect is more than my superior scientific mind can endure!
LiberalEvent2_003=No, it is clear they are attempting to weasel money from our coffers. His insinuation that we have not yet provided sufficient impetus to sway his political decisiveness is well understood. If we would like to see our choice become law, we need to offer a bribe.
LiberalEvent2_004=A bribe of **${bribed}** will be sufficient. Otherwise we can allow the people to make the choice.

# passages/00086-LiberalEventA.mws.yaml
LiberalEventA_001=Estate Taxes
LiberalEventA_004=A new "income tax" has been created to reduce the proper stratification of society by wealth seen across Transylvania. It naturally disgusts me, but I find it better than the alternative.
LiberalEventA_005=Each player **must pay $1** to the supply.

# passages/00087-LiberalEventB.mws.yaml
LiberalEventB_001=Ethnic Separatism
LiberalEventB_002=The Nationalist movement within parliament is successful. I find myself unmoved by the horrifying details of conditions within the Asylum worsening and deportations of various peoples based on their ethnic group or religious views. Politics. It will sort itself out.
LiberalEventB_003=**Each player must return their {asylumup} tile to the Scenario box.**

# passages/00088-SmugEvent.mws.yaml
SmugEvent_001=**Carefully pick up the Storybook device and hand it to the player with the least VP.** _If there is a tie, hand this to the one who was later in turn order in the previous round._ **This passage is read in full view of all players.**
SmugEvent_002=**A Controlled Release**
SmugEvent_003=My cousins and I have come to an agreement as of earlier today; one that I believe we should have spoken of much sooner. The topic came about as we were discussing our various sundry interests, and like the pendulum tick of a longcase clock, our words kept returning to the stifling environment in which we now found ourselves.
SmugEvent_004=I'll be quick with it; we resolved to turn a resounding negative into a boon!
SmugEvent_005=One of the distinct bonuses of being located near an entire town surrounded by a large wall is that it provides excellent controls for an experiment. Without the means to escape, our scientific methods could be indulged with little consequence.
SmugEvent_006=**Choose!**
SmugEvent_007=Retrieve the 3 **Collaborative Experiments** from the Scenario box.
SmugEvent_008=The player with the **least VP** now chooses the **type** of Collaborative Experiment that all players will be working towards. This determines which of the three Experiments will be unleashed. _To be completed, this Experiment will require multiple players to complete Experiments of that type this round._
SmugEvent_009=Complete a Biology Experiment.
SmugEvent_011=Complete a Chemistry Experiment.
SmugEvent_013=Complete an Engineering Experiment.

# passages/00089-SmugEventA.mws.yaml
SmugEventA_002=To properly introduce the creation to a captive audience, **{collab}** Collaboration {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} tokens must be gained by completing 
SmugEventA_003=an Engineering
SmugEventA_004=a Biology
SmugEventA_005=a Chemistry
SmugEventA_006= Experiment. 
SmugEventA_007=Each player can only gain **1** Collaboration token {icon:s2_collaborativetoken}.
SmugEventA_008=The player who gains the most {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} tokens will gain an additional **4VP.**
SmugEventA_009=Place the 
SmugEventA_010=**A Robot Servant That Prepares Meals with Lasers**
SmugEventA_011=**Injecting an Agitated Gorilla with Hormones and Radium**
SmugEventA_012=**A Fabric That Cannot Become Stained**
SmugEventA_013= Experiment face-up on the table. Discard the remaining Collaborative Experiments.
SmugEventA_014=Then, retrieve **{collab}** {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} tokens and place them on the Collaborative Experiment.
SmugEventA_015=**WARNING: COMPLETING THIS EXPERIMENT WILL DEFINITELY DESTROY CITY HALL. MEANING THAT YOU WILL NOT HAVE TO PLACE YOUR SELF TOKEN ONTO IT. ALSO, IT MAY HAVE OTHER, MORE DIRE CONSEQUENCES.**

# passages/00090-SmugConsequence.mws.yaml
SmugConsequence_001=Consequences of Smuggling
SmugConsequence_002=This fortified district offers little in the way of investment, so I'm afraid to admit that I have begun a partnership with the local shipping company. What it lacks in potential, I believe it makes up for in expediency. I swear to you my visits there are brief and lawful, for I am as always a dutiful citizen.
SmugConsequence_003=What is this place? It is certainly not much from the exterior, but considering the locale, I have very little choice in the matter. It provides me access to goods otherwise inaccessible, and while the stench is sometimes severe - both of the building and its inhabitants - this is all I require.
SmugConsequence_004=I ask you to disregard the rumors that I have merely invested capital into this venture to gain illicit produce. It is a humble shipping dock and my visits during the evening are simply to assess matters of inventory. I take offense to any suggestions otherwise.
SmugConsequence_005=**Please choose your name and add it to the ledger:**

# passages/00091-S4Con2A.mws.yaml
S4Con2A_001=Success
S4Con2A_002=Shameful Display
S4Con2A_003=**Letter from {tempid}-** _(Cont.)_
S4Con2A_004=My representation was easily able to refute the validity of several eyewitness accounts from slipshod drunkards, but the court proceedings dragged on for several months.
S4Con2A_005=Ultimately, the blasted dullards had not a leg to stand on and were forced to drop the case entirely. While the court costs are minor and the fines insignificant, the time wasted in this extended defense and the indigestion I have endured has caused my work to suffer.
S4Con2A_006=You **lose {_rnd_S4Con2A_0}VP**.
S4Con2A_007=Despite circumstantial evidence, the town's courts were unable to reconcile their case with my unusual investment practices. Several witnesses attested to my family's eccentric habits, and while it does not put the courts at ease, the argument is compelling enough for them to drop the charges without fines.
S4Con2A_008=You should have seen the unsteadiness of the case they brought against me! Several witnesses attested to my connection to the local smuggling ring (absurd), but the bedraggled individuals could not even keep their own stories straight. 
S4Con2A_009=We are dealing with the simple-minded, however. The judge, in their folly, determined that scant evidence was significant enough to damn me. While the court costs are minor and the fines insignificant, the resulting public backlash will certainly hamper my ability to complete any work in peace.
S4Con2A_010=You **lose 1VP** and **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.
S4Con2A_011=**Letter from {tempid} -** _(Cont.)_

# passages/00092-TensionBonus.mws.yaml
TensionBonus_001=Cabinet of Curiosities
TensionBonus_002=Award the player(s) with the most completed **Occult** Experiments the **Cabinet of Curiosities** Vanity Estate Upgrade. 
TensionBonus_003= _Ties are broken by the one with the lowest VP. If there is still a tie, it is broken by the one who went last in the final round._
TensionBonus_004=**Also,** any player who has completed their **Occult Journal Track** **gains 3VP**.

# passages/00093-LiberalBonus.mws.yaml
LiberalBonus_002=The **Menagerie** Estate Upgrade is now awarded to the player with the most completed {mentype} Experiments. _If there is a tie, the one with lowest VP receives the Upgrade._ 
LiberalBonus_003=The player who has the second-most Experiments also gains this Upgrade.

# passages/00094-SmugEvent2.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2_001=A Controlled Experiment
SmugEvent2_002=Did {collab} Players collect **Collaboration tokens**{icon:s2_collaborativetoken}?
SmugEvent2_003=Were all the **Collaboration tokens**{icon:s2_collaborativetoken} collected?

# passages/00095-SmugEvent2A.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2A_001=Town Hall Destroyed
SmugEvent2A_002=**Newsprint - {newspaper} -** _15 March, 1912._
SmugEvent2A_003=Four dead and several injured after a calamity of epic proportions occurred yesterday in our fair city of {townname}. While the cause of the sudden implosion and subsequent spread of detritus remains unknown, officials confirm the complete destruction of the Town Hall.
SmugEvent2A_004=The player with the most Collaboration tokens {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} **gains 4VP**. 
SmugEvent2A_005={nameA} loses **{tempcreep}**{icon:creepy_icon}.
SmugEvent2A_006=Players that have already visited the Town Hall gain a small bonus:
SmugEvent2A_007={nameB} loses **{tempcreep}**{icon:creepy_icon}.
SmugEvent2A_008={nameC} loses **{tempcreep}**{icon:creepy_icon}.
SmugEvent2A_009={nameD} loses **{tempcreep}**{icon:creepy_icon}.
SmugEvent2A_010={nameE} loses **{tempcreep}**{icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00096-SmugEvent2B.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2B_001=Missed Opportunity
SmugEvent2B_002=I knew it would never amount to anything! My cousins do not share the same illumination, the same pioneering spirit that I exhibit! They would rather languish in gluttony and submit to the oppressive state. I see their bellies grow rotund in their slothful lethargy, their porcine features stuffed into last year's fashion by couturiers no doubt pushed to the brink.
SmugEvent2B_003=Perhaps it was good that they could not complete it. At least that way the experiment could not be considered a _failure_!
SmugEvent2B_004=Any player who gained a Collaboration token {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} gains **1 Knowledge of their choice**
SmugEvent2B_005= for each
SmugEvent2B_006= and then returns the token to the box.
SmugEvent2B_007=Any player who does not have a Collaboration token {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} is not dedicated to the craft and **loses 2VP**.
SmugEvent2B_008=The player with the most Collaboration tokens {icon:s2_collaborativetoken} **gains 4VP**. _If there is a tie, no one receives this bonus._

# passages/00097-SmugEvent2Aa.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2Aa_003=The Bank was the next target of our experiment's seemingly arbitrary rage. Perhaps it was the promise of glittering treasures within that caught its attention; or more likely, it was the soldier stationed out front who fired upon it repeatedly with a handgun.
SmugEvent2Aa_004=Either way, the soldier was given a premature burial under the falling stone and girders that burst from the structure as it was torn apart quite violently and the path of rampage continued.

# passages/00098-SmugEvent2aa.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2aa_001=It was unfortunate to see the library - however limited its collection and provisional its overall design - collapse into a pile of dust, books, and blood.
SmugEvent2aa_002=Our creation paused for a brief moment, the entirety of its form shaking violently in the center of the town. Suddenly, with a blinding flash and a resultant shockwave which shattered the windows of all nearby business, it exploded. The vibrant display was admittedly so engrossing that for a moment I imagined the townsfolk had simply been stunned into silence. At least until several spontaneously burst into flames.
SmugEvent2aa_003=With nowhere to escape, the remaining townsfolk desperately attempted to douse the fires and rush to the aide of the injured. We watched from our cliffside seclusion as pandemonium gripped the populace.
SmugEvent2aa_004=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker **3 spaces** to the left.

# passages/00099-S4Kill2.mws.yaml
S4Kill2_001=Accuse!
S4Kill2_004=YAY: Vote to kill the **Blacksmith.**
S4Kill2_005=NAY: Vote to kill the **Butcher.**
S4Kill2_006=Tally the vote count _(ties are broken by the player who went last this round)._
S4Kill2_007=Click to start the vote...

# passages/00100-SmugEventEnd.mws.yaml
SmugEventEnd_001=The Rampage Concludes
SmugEventEnd_002=Disappointingly, the action ceased just as quickly as it had begun. 
SmugEventEnd_003=Our Robot expeled a burst of steam that sent a nearby crowd screaming and clutching at their eyes, before its clockwork form began to seize up in the center of the street.
SmugEventEnd_004=Our Gorilla, now grown to the size of a small home, beat its mighty fists against its chest one last time with a roar that rattled our inner ears even from nearly a kilometer away. It then struggled for balance.
SmugEventEnd_005=The Fabric swirled one last time in the air, launching a pedestrian with such force that their ragdoll form cleared the exterior wall of the town. A streak of electricity flashed once upon its surface and it began to lazily descend as if caught in a gust of wind.
SmugEventEnd_006=Our creation settled lifelessly to the ground, bits of metal, wood, and smoldering flesh strewn about the cobblestones where it lay. While we would have enjoyed seeing our experiment tested at the highest level, the cloud of smoke and the destruction left in its wake were acceptable.
SmugEventEnd_007=The townsfolk scrambled through the streets trying to put out fires that popped up throughout the town as we enjoyed a warm coffee from our secluded viewing location and discussed the results. Science can be so satisfying.
SmugEventEnd_008=1 space
SmugEventEnd_009=2 spaces
SmugEventEnd_010=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker **{_rnd_SmugEventEnd_0}** to the left.

# passages/00101-LiberalTaxes.mws.yaml
LiberalTaxes_001=Death and Taxes
LiberalTaxes_002=Taxes upon an inheritance? Have you heard of such a thing? It appears that the county exchequer has levied an estate tax upon the wealthier citizenry.
LiberalTaxes_003=Our mid-morning bout of croquet was unduly interrupted by the arrival of the news. This progressive poppycock was so destructive to my ability to run the hoop that my spouse was able to peg out well before I was competitive. Does an estate mean nothing to these leeches?
LiberalTaxes_004=They claim it is necessary to ensure the Asylum and various other modern amenities like public schools and health care are provided. Perhaps if they ran these facilities profitably they would not have to bleed their constituents.
LiberalTaxes_005=It took several days of constitutional rest for my spouse and I to recover from the shock of this intrusion into our financial affairs!

# passages/00102-LiberalTaxes2.mws.yaml
LiberalTaxes2_001=Seizure of Goods or Trade
LiberalTaxes2_002=In the coming weeks, several armed men along with a single gentleman dressed in a brown sack suit arrived at the estates of my cousins who chose to avoid tax collection.
LiberalTaxes2_003=Any player who **paid their taxes** in full, gains **{_rnd_LiberalTaxes2_0}VP** immediately.
LiberalTaxes2_004=Any player who **refused** to pay taxes may immediately make up the difference by returning **1 Ingredient OR 1 Estate Upgrade to the supply for every 2 Estate Upgrades they own.** If they cannot or choose not to perform this action, they must **place their Self on the City Hall immediately and Lose {_rnd_LiberalTaxes2_1}VP**. _This token performs no action this round._

# passages/00103-WallEvent2.mws.yaml
WallEvent2_001=A Vague Promise
WallEvent2_002=The effect of our decision was not immediately apparent, but I could discern that the townspeople were grateful for support from the aristocracy.
WallEvent2_003=The Romani caravans, while still apprehensive, seem to have recognized the sincerity of our deeds, or the depth of our pockets. Whether trust has been gained or a mutually beneficial arrangement, I suspect they will return again at a later date and reward the members of our family with weaker hearts. 
WallEvent2_004=Click to continue…
WallEvent2_005=All players with money in their hand must pay it to the supply to gain a **Memorial Brick**. They immediately gain **2VP** and **lose 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**
WallEvent2_006=Retrieve the **Market tokens** {icon:s2_markettoken} from the Scenario box.
WallEvent2_007=Any player who did **not** build a piece of the wall gains a **Market token**{icon:s2_markettoken}.
WallEvent2_008=**For the remainder of the game, at the end of each round, there is a chance that the Romani will visit the town and offer goods to players with a {icon:s2_markettoken} token.**
WallEvent2_009=In the coming weeks, the traveling caravans kept their distance, unsure of the new direction the town had taken. However, on the occasions that I frequented their motley convoy they pledged to return again at a later date and reward the members of our family with weaker hearts.
WallEvent2_010=All players with money in their hand must pay it to the supply to gain a **Memorial Brick**. They immediately gain **2VP** and **lose 1** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**
WallEvent2_011=Any player who did **not** spend $1 for a brick, gains **1 Occult Knowledge** and a **Market token** {icon:s2_markettoken}. 
WallEvent2_012=**For the remainder of the game, at the end of each round there is a chance that the Romani will visit the town and offer goods to players with a {icon:s2_markettoken} token.**

# passages/00104-Caravansery.mws.yaml
Caravansery_001=A Visit From the Caravans
Caravansery_002=A brightly colored carriage arrived today. Its occupants quickly dislodged themselves and through a series of minor alterations, the shutters of the wagon were opened to create an informal display counter with a fabric awning above. Against the monochrome and misty gray stone of the castle walls, the impromptu market looked positively alluring.
Caravansery_004=In turn order, any player with a **Market token** {icon:s2_markettoken} may choose to purchase **any number** of goods at the Traveling Caravan:
Caravansery_005=**Pay $1: Gain 1 Ingredient or 1 Knowledge of your choice.**
Caravansery_006=_We note that the caravan is always wandering and is never guaranteed to return again._

# passages/00106-NameEntryA.mws.yaml
NameEntryA_002={nameA}.
NameEntryA_003=Our warmest regards.

# passages/00107-NameEntryB.mws.yaml
NameEntryB_001={nameB}.
NameEntryB_002=Please enjoy your experience.

# passages/00108-NameEntryC.mws.yaml
NameEntryC_001={nameC}.
NameEntryC_002=May your name live in infamy.

# passages/00109-NameEntryD.mws.yaml
NameEntryD_001={nameD}.

# passages/00110-NameEntryE.mws.yaml
NameEntryE_001={nameE}.

# passages/00111-IntroNameEntry.mws.yaml
IntroNameEntry_001=Proper Nomenclature
IntroNameEntry_006=As siblings of an influential family of Eastern European descent, the **{playtxt}** of us have received a not insignificant portion of our family's estate.
IntroNameEntry_007=Before we begin, let us make this historical fiction more engaging by providing our names.

# passages/00112-EssentialSalts.mws.yaml
EssentialSalts_001=Hope Springs Eternal
EssentialSalts_002=The package has arrived! The vial of essential salts is well and fully intact with a cork stopper firmly fastened. It is as diminutive as I expected, with a small tag attached displaying an Enochian phrase, "Yogg-Sothoth Neblod Zin."
EssentialSalts_003=Afternoon Note: Initial experiments have proven promising. A rabbit, only days since skinned and left to drain. The formulae recommended by Joseph Curwen caused a green-black smoke to arise around the carcass. But, moments later, I saw the beating of the animal's once-dead heart as it began to struggle against its bindings! Life from death!
EssentialSalts_004=With the creature lain to rest, there is nothing preventing me from achieving what I have desired for so long! To resurrect my love and return to the happiness we once shared!

# passages/00113-EssentialCons.mws.yaml
EssentialCons_003=With a billow of emerald smoke, I saw the features of my long-dead spouse reform into the perfect form I remembered from my youth. I had done it!
EssentialCons_004=However, I find that their temperament is uneven. On one particular evening, they suddenly burst open the doors of our carriage and fled into an alleyway before I could recover my senses enough to make chase.
EssentialCons_005=I observed in abject horror as their neck spun unnaturally around to face me while their body remained stationary. Their feral lips were covered in blood and the fresh body of some unfortunate man lay eviscerated on the cobblestones, their insides glistening in the haze of a crescent moon.
EssentialCons_006=Generally though, they are back to their normal selves.
EssentialCons_007=I could scarcely trust my own senses. It worked? And without any defects visible or otherwise?
EssentialCons_008=I embraced them, and though they were startled by the decades' difference in our ages, they returned the embrace. I am a genius!
EssentialCons_009=Any player who chose to perform the resurrection **regains their Spouse** from the game box and places it in their Quarters.
EssentialCons_010=They also **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon} and **1** {icon:bodies_icon}**.**

# passages/00114-EssentialSaltsRes.mws.yaml
EssentialSaltsRes_001=With a billow of emerald smoke, I saw the features of my long-dead spouse begin to reform.
EssentialSaltsRes_002=However, the hideous silhouette that emerged from within the shroud of electrical mist only vaguely resembled my lost love. Their skin oozed about their unsettling musculature while they rose to their feet with a hunched back and a stiff gait on legs of different lengths.
EssentialSaltsRes_003=I spoke to them and though the torment of existence wore heavily on their shambling form, my spouse returned a toothless smile and dutifully obeyed my commands.
EssentialSaltsRes_004=Any player who chose to perform the resurrection **gains a Caretaker from Lost** and **2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**
EssentialSaltsRes_005=_If you cannot gain a Caretaker from Lost,_ **gain 2VP, 1** {icon:bodies_icon}**, and 2** {icon:creepy_icon} _instead._

# passages/00115-Variable_List_FnP.mws.yaml
Variable_List_FnP_001={nameA}/B/C/D/E = chosen name of player
Variable_List_FnP_002={players} = number of players
Variable_List_FnP_003={playtxt} = text version of number of players
Variable_List_FnP_004={randomplayer} = array of current player names
Variable_List_FnP_005={randomname} = used with above for random name.
Variable_List_FnP_006={townname} = name of the village in the game
Variable_List_FnP_007={nameA} II (remember to make it the second for Gen 2)
Variable_List_FnP_008={nameA} III (remember to make it the third for Gen 3)

# passages/00116-WitchIsolationResolution.mws.yaml
WitchIsolationResolution_001=Minor Recompense
WitchIsolationResolution_003=The townsfolk are wary of me. As well they should be. While I do not hold grudges against simpletons unworthy of my time, the death of my parent is a wound that festers deep within me and I feel no sense of pride in this place.
WitchIsolationResolution_004=I am left to my own dark devices, sequestered in my study with dusty tomes and ancient scrolls. My work is my rebellion against their oppression. If the city burns, I will not fan the flames, but I will watch it roast.
WitchIsolationResolution_005={witch} gains 1 {icon:creepy_icon} and 2 Knowledge of their choice.

# passages/00117-WitchTensionResolution.mws.yaml
WitchTensionResolution_001=Reconciliation
WitchTensionResolution_002=The townsfolk feel a kinship with my family's unnatural suffering. As well they should. The death of my parent is a wound that festers deep within me and I feel no sense of pride in this place. 
WitchTensionResolution_003=A brief visit to their grave - the mausoleum nestled within our family's cemetery plot - reminds me of this grim distance.
WitchTensionResolution_004=Yet, it would be unwise of me not to accept their pledge of service, even while the grief still hangs like a sullen fog above the shattered fragments of my tortured soul.
WitchTensionResolution_005={witch} gains a Servant from Lost and 1 Ingredient of their choice. _If you have no Servants available in Lost, gain 2VP instead._

# passages/00118-TenseEventBad2.mws.yaml
TenseEventBad2_001=Ways to Ease the Tension
TenseEventBad2_002=I have peered into the darkness and seen the blackness of men's souls. They shamble forward in my dreams, like fresh corpses wreathed in a haze of putrefaction. Their cold hands clutch at my nightgown. When they have surrounded me fully with their numbers, filling my vision with a wall of decaying flesh - that is when I awake again, screaming.
TenseEventBad2_003=These recurring dreams only amplify the anxiety I feel when I peer out my window and observe the icy gray village I once loved. Their betrayal has left me in desolate isolation, deprived of access to the resources I require. If only they could see the worth in my experiments. If only they knew how much I wallow in anguish for their sake!
TenseEventBad2_004=They have already pushed me this far, why should I be denied the resources for which I am so desperate? Even if I must retrieve them through more venomous means, I am firm in my convictions. But I will need the help of my cousins to complete this task. I plan to write them on the morrow!

# passages/00119-NOTEforthissection.mws.yaml
NOTEforthissection_001=Components:
NOTEforthissection_002=Lost Tile - for Asylum
NOTEforthissection_003=Business Building in Country
NOTEforthissection_004=New Asylum Pages
NOTEforthissection_005=BALL AND CHAIN NOT USED
NOTEforthissection_006=BALL & Chain side-quest.
NOTEforthissection_007=Notes to TC-
NOTEforthissection_008=What has the government done for us lately? Nothing
NOTEforthissection_009=I may be able to wrestle the strict government control over this fine establishment and put the matter into private hands. Nothing more rehabilitating than hard work and an honest wage. And I am sure that you would enjoy some
NOTEforthissection_010=Possibly place a new building outside town near the table. Go have a meeting out there. OR you can visit the Asylum and have a meeting there. OR Both. Whatever you like.
NOTEforthissection_011=Obsession Cards given
NOTEforthissection_012=Creature Appears
NOTEforthissection_013=Asylum Opens - flip to Asylum Lost - (If Butcher was killed, all players return one Servant (not Spouse) to Lost if possible.)
NOTEforthissection_014=Opportunity arises at the House on the Hill - Sells work-release Estate Upgrade.
NOTEforthissection_015=Support the Asylum Project as successful. OR deem it unnecessary.
NOTEforthissection_016=First to visit the House on the Hill token!
NOTEforthissection_017=End of Gen. - SPLIT
NOTEforthissection_018=How many people supported Business?
NOTEforthissection_019=Did we complete the Creature's request?
NOTEforthissection_020=Could provide sign in for Creature
NOTEforthissection_021=SOMEONE could NAME the Asylum after the Butcher or the Blacksmith. Amelia Fischer & Cedric Mayer
NOTEforthissection_022=What IF LOST becomes the Asylum?
NOTEforthissection_023=Players, if they have any Servants, lose one to the Asylum when it opens.
NOTEforthissection_024=Asylum is -2 Sanity.
NOTEforthissection_025=Businessman invites them to the hills to his home for a secret meeting.
NOTEforthissection_026=Change Moguls to those interested in swaying us toward rehabilitation.
NOTEforthissection_027=Will we help build the Asylum by investing capital?
NOTEforthissection_028=Can patients really be rehabilitated? Can WE be rehabilitated?
NOTEforthissection_029=How could we SHOW how rehabilitated we are? Or how rehabilitated the patients are?
NOTEforthissection_030=For Fame
NOTEforthissection_031=For Knowledge
NOTEforthissection_032=For Science
NOTEforthissection_033=For Revenge
NOTEforthissection_034=For Respect

# passages/00120-Guilt.mws.yaml
Guilt_001=Wracked with Guilt
Guilt_002=Creating life against my will only to feed the urges of a hideous fiend? Am I forced to forever suffer for the sins of my family? What good can come from aiding the devil's work?
Guilt_003=I curse my grandfather for thrusting this abomination into the world and dooming us to accommodate its unnatural wants. Oh, how the sorrow encompasses me!
Guilt_004=The experiment is complete, but I cannot bear to look upon it! What foul work! I have remained in my bedchamber for weeks in a wretched state of remorse. But, when I emerge from my infernal cocoon of solitude, I will rip that cursed page from my journal and throw it hence into the fireplace.
Guilt_005=**Move backwards 1 space on a Journal Track of your choice.** _If this movement would cause you to move from Level 3 to Level 2, you must return a Vanity Upgrade you have built to the supply. If you cannot move backwards any spaces, lose 4VP._
Guilt_006=Then, collect the card and keep it face-up in your play area as a completed Experiment.

# passages/00121-WitchIntro2.mws.yaml
WitchIntro2_001=A Game of Hexes
WitchIntro2_002=**One of the players may be cursed.**
WitchIntro2_003=**One of the players has become cursed.**
WitchIntro2_004=To test the theory and attempt to discover the affected individual, my cousins and I have decided to **hex** a building in town. If the building we marked in our mind truly became dangerous, we would repeat the process to conclude who is the cursed cousin. 
WitchIntro2_005=or if the {wsuspect} is simply attempting to deepen the paranoia within {townname} with their actions
WitchIntro2_006=How droll!
WitchIntro2_007=Turn to page **13** of the Village Chronicle.
WitchIntro2_008=Turn to page **12** of the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00122-86NoteWrit.mws.yaml
_86NoteWrit_001=CLICK HERE.
_86NoteWrit_002=Could all players be killed instead if they are wrong in total? That would be "fun."
_86NoteWrit_003=Could it be that one of us is responsible for this admittedly amusing bit of deception? With the knowledge of my parent's secrets, could I even trust my own innocence?
_86NoteWrit_004=Again, their terminology of "city" is very loose considering the dimimunative census numbers and declining economic situation. However, placing blame on several moorish inhabitants and traveling Romani caravans has created an ignorant though soothing effect. If their is built, however, our access to occult research may become extremely limited.
_86NoteWrit_005=Though the aims of the men orchestrating the political manuever remained dubious, s
_86NoteWrit_006=If the structure is built.
_86NoteWrit_007= The town remembers the dark past, and does not remember an Angry Mob at our doorstep.
_86NoteWrit_008= The town still talks about the village's angry mobs knocking at our grandparents' gates.

# passages/00123-CommemorativeIntro.mws.yaml
CommemorativeIntro_001=Strengthening the Town
CommemorativeIntro_002=**Letter from** **{randomname} -** _27 August, 1862._
CommemorativeIntro_003=Despite the gloom and hysterical accusations, I have noticed a growing movement for a return to stability and to celebrate what makes the town of {townname} unique. Though I am sure these dim souls haven't quite determined what that means exactly, they are raising funds for the vague plans of a memorial.
CommemorativeIntro_004=Doomed to failure, most likely. However, if having my initials inscribed onto a brick could somehow chase away the rabble from my doorstep, I may reluctantly oblige.
CommemorativeIntro_005=During this Generation, players may visit the Town Hall to purchase a commemorative brick for the new memorial. The cost is $2 or placing a Servant into Lost. Bricks are placed near the player's Estate.
CommemorativeIntro_006=Each Memorial Brick is worth **{brickvalue}VP** upon purchase. At the End of the Generation, the player who has the most bricks receives the **Key to the City** Upgrade. _Ties are broken by the player with the fewest VP._ 

# passages/00124-WallEvent1.mws.yaml
WallEvent1_001=Opportunity
WallEvent1_002=Each player is given an opportunity to purchase a **Memorial Brick** at a price of $1. To help boost our decision to aide, the representatives promise to spread word about our contribution _(we will gain_ **2VP** _and_ **lose 2** {icon:creepy_icon}_)._
WallEvent1_003=The Romani cannot offer much to sway our decision, despite a promise to offer an attractive array of exotic goods to anyone who shows support for their continued inclusion by denying this vote.
WallEvent1_004=**Monetary VOTE**
WallEvent1_005=All players take all their money into their hands.
WallEvent1_006=**If they wish to buy a brick,** they secretly place $1 into one closed fist and extend it to the center of the table.
WallEvent1_007=**If they wish to abstain,** they secretly extend an empty closed fist to the center of the table. When all players have decided, all players reveal their choices simultaneously.

# passages/00125-F8Note.mws.yaml
F8Note_001=Add Resolution of some sort:
F8Note_002=Resolution for Witch Escaping?
F8Note_003=The Witch player was not found. No bonus. Potentially visited by interested parties.
F8Note_004=Could ADD alternative Market token bonus if {wall} is yes or no.

# passages/00127-Tension3.mws.yaml
Tension3_001={icon:storybooktoken} **A Crossroads**
Tension3_002=**Obsession Penalty**
Tension3_003=Any player who does not Deepen their Obsession by the End of this Generation will **lose {obsvp}VP.**

# passages/00128-TenseConfirm.mws.yaml
TenseConfirm_001=Calm Before the Tempest
TenseConfirm_002=There is something strange in the air. I cannot discern a difference in barometric pressure, nor does the weather conflict with the season. Still, I feel a tension that rattles the fillings in my molars. There is a change on the horizon.
TenseConfirm_003=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker to the same space as the Romani token {icon:s2_romanitoken} , then remove the Romani token {icon:s2_romanitoken} from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.
TenseConfirm_004=Remove the Romani token {icon:s2_romanitoken} from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.
TenseConfirm_006=The {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker will remain where it is until the end of the round. Ignore any ability or effect that would move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker.

# passages/00129-FP10VP.mws.yaml
FP10VP_001=Ceaseless Ambition
FP10VP_002=**Choose your player name and begin your destiny:**

# passages/00130-FPResearch2.mws.yaml
FPResearch2_001=Boundless Study

# passages/00131-FPSanity3.mws.yaml
FPSanity3_001=Pressing the Boundaries

# passages/00132-FPCreepy3.mws.yaml
FPCreepy3_001=Feared and Misunderstood

# passages/00133-FPYesHub.mws.yaml
FPYesHub_001=Destiny Awaits
FPYesHub_002=Your choice has been made.
FPYesHub_003=**Immediately Gain 1VP.**

# passages/00134-FPResearch2signin.mws.yaml
FPResearch2signin_001=The New Science
FPResearch2signin_002=**Newsprint - {newspaper} -** _2 April, 1861._
FPResearch2signin_003=Yesterday evening, a local aristocrat and inventor received the first annual achievement award in science for their distinguished work. The award was presented during a ceremony on their newly renovated grounds which overlook the village of {townname}.
FPResearch2signin_004=Upon accepting the award from the University of Iaşi, the fellow made these remarks: "I want to advance Science at all costs. No mountain is too high. No religious or ethical boundary too compelling. My important work will usher in a new age - the Age of SCIENCE!"
FPResearch2signin_005=Return all {icon:storybooktoken} tokens on all player's **Journal** Tracks to the box.

# passages/00135-FPSanity3signin.mws.yaml
FPSanity3signin_001=Dedication Should Not Be Punished
FPSanity3signin_002=**Anonymous Editorial - {newspaper} -** _18 July, 1860._
FPSanity3signin_003=The level of paranoia I have witnessed among the townsfolk would be unfathomable if I had not seen it with my own eyes. I believe - as an anonymous and unbiased person without any scientific background - it is of utmost importance for us to push past these ridiculous preconceptions and expand our acceptance of new ideas.
FPSanity3signin_004=Who are we to judge a person for returning to the same shop several times in a week to purchase a live rabbit? Or to peruse the caravans for curiosities and trinkets? Who among us has not spent several dark evenings contemplating their existence among the graves in the cemetery?
FPSanity3signin_005=A person should be judged by their results, not by the means by which they achieve them.

# passages/00136-FPCreepy3signin.mws.yaml
FPCreepy3signin_001=A Town's Suspicions
FPCreepy3signin_002=An Interview
FPCreepy3signin_003=**Excerpt - {newspaper} -** _23 February, 1861._
FPCreepy3signin_004=...I decided to ask about more pressing matters and several behavior complaints logged by citizens at the local town hall. However, as I was about to make my inquiry, a black carriage rode by and both passenger and driver alike made stern looks in our direction.
FPCreepy3signin_005=It appeared this treatment was enough for my companion to throw down their handkerchief and look towards the sky with menace. "How dare they turn their sullen glances towards me! I'll show them. I'll show them all!" The regal entrepreneur then let out a hearty laugh which both confused and delighted passersby. I decided to assume this was a cue to postpone any further interview when the laughter continued for several minutes unabated.

# passages/00137-FPNo.mws.yaml
FPNo_001=Overambitious
FPNo_002=**Journal of {tempname} -** _September, 1839. Romania._
FPNo_003=Even having already determined my fate, I was still unable to control my ambitious impulses. Curse my own ceaseless ambition!
FPNo_004=Today, the townspeople whispered as I walked by. They distrust the science I am perfecting. They make casual accusations of vile acts which I could not repeat in writing. I have resigned myself to retreating to my estate for now. Away from the prying eyes and chattering gossip of the peasantry.
FPNo_005=**Immediately gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}**.** The token remains where it is, until another player claims it.

# passages/00139-ManiaSpecial.mws.yaml
ManiaSpecial_001=Shared Mania
ManiaSpecial_002=**Journal Entry -** **{randomname} -** _14 July, 1831._
ManiaSpecial_003=The cold and dark landscape should by all accounts be an affront to my demeanor - and it certainly is to my spouse - but I find myself rejuvenated in a way that beguiles my rational mind. They say that ashes can enrich the soil and make the next harvest stronger. Well, if the grayness of this countryside serves as an ample fertilizer, my mind is a germinating seed ready to burst from the Earth.
ManiaSpecial_004=This collective mania - it is contagious. Each day I find my mind wandering, dreaming up new formulas and calculations, drafting notes as if possessed by some unseen force. For now, I will let my thoughts go wherever they are wont to go.
ManiaSpecial_005=However, I will find my true calling. In this frenzied era of wild ideas and incendiary superstitions, I will emerge focused and determined!
ManiaSpecial_006=**Retrieve the {icon:storybooktoken} tokens.**
ManiaSpecial_007=Place a{icon:storybooktoken}token on
ManiaSpecial_008=**space 10** of the Victory Point Track.
ManiaSpecial_009=**space 3** of the {icon:insanity_icon} Track.
ManiaSpecial_010=**space 3** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.
ManiaSpecial_011=All players place a{icon:storybooktoken}token on the top of their
ManiaSpecial_012=**2nd Level Journal** column.
ManiaSpecial_013=When a player's piece reaches one of these tokens, they will click on the appropriate link and receive a special message for this achievement.

# passages/00140-FP1OverBonus.mws.yaml
FP1OverBonus_001=Over-Achievement
FP1OverBonus_002=**Journal of** _name illegible - September, 1839. Romania._
FP1OverBonus_003=I am nothing if not thorough.
FP1OverBonus_004=I sometimes cannot contain my genius.
FP1OverBonus_005={_rnd_FP1OverBonus_0} While I had already chosen my path towards destiny, I find it exceedingly fruitful to bask in a brief affirmation of my own self-worth. I awake each day and throw open the curtains, letting the ashen fog roll by, invigorated at the prospects of what scientific ventures lay before me. Even in this tense climate of murky paranoia, it is comforting to revel in the minor victories.
FP1OverBonus_006=**Immediately Gain 3VP** and return the token(s) to the box.

# passages/00142-FP10VPsignin.mws.yaml
FP10VPsignin_001=Local Inventor Sees Meteoric Rise
FP10VPsignin_003=A local entrepreneur and inventor has recently caught the eye of the populace, for better or worse. While their experimentations have become public due to their loud and extravagant nature, this ambition has caused old questions to resurface as to the family's legacy in the region.
FP10VPsignin_004=The entrepreneurs' spirit has been on record at several occasions in recent history. "I want fame and fortune," the aristocrat proclaimed without prompting. "So I will have it. Let them watch the future unfold before their eyes!" It is of our opinion, that with tensions on the rise, perhaps these sentiments were best kept muted.

# passages/00143-TheCreatureCard.mws.yaml
TheCreatureCard_001=The Creature
TheCreatureCard_002=**Brief Journal Excerpt -** **{randomname} -** _4 March 1863._
TheCreatureCard_003=The unexpected presence of the malformed creature stunned the family and shocked my senses. Is it possible that these were not merely "plans and sketches" passed down to us through the generations, but the horrible realization of an experiment of our grandfather's?
TheCreatureCard_004=Does any player have **The Creature Masterwork Experiment**?

# passages/00144-TheCreatureCard2.mws.yaml
TheCreatureCard2_001=Hideous Motivation
TheCreatureCard2_002=**Brief Journal Excerpt -** _(date and name illegible)_
TheCreatureCard2_003=I knew now that I could not sit idly by, knowing that my grandfather's amazing failure was creeping around the countryside. I resolved to assess and improve my family's technique and create a true Masterwork that would secure our legacy.
TheCreatureCard2_005=Retrieve **The Creature Masterwork Upgrade** card from the Scenario box. Then, give it to the player with **THE CREATURE** Masterwork Experiment. This card goes into effect immediately and must be kept face-up near that player's Estate for the remainder of the game.

# passages/00145-AsylumOpps.mws.yaml
AsylumOpps_001=The Esteemed Institution
AsylumOpps_002=If you are not already aware, the new Asylum has begun operations. Naturally, I encountered my dear cousins at the ribbon-cutting ceremony just weeks ago. As was customary during these sorts of celebrations, the mayor of {townname} was dolefully in attendance, as were several visiting dignitaries of various unimportance.
AsylumOpps_003=If it weren't enough to stunt my studies with niceties, the event that followed a few days later served to compound my annoyance with this pseudoscience. One of my servants had willingly admitted themselves to this untested facility! And after all the care I had given them!
AsylumOpps_004=I fear I will be forced to visit this place now. Perhaps the introduction of these alienist philosophies will soothe my anxieties. Ha! I chortled so hard at that I nearly spilt my brandy upon the page.
AsylumOpps_005=Each player must **return a Servant to Lost**.

# passages/00146-BusinessMeet.mws.yaml
BusinessMeet_001=Meeting on the Hill
BusinessMeet_002=With distinct gothic style, a robust gate and fencing stretching the perimeter of the plot and an entryway leading towards a dual staircase carpetted with crimson linens of the finest quality, the decor struck me as appropriately imposing.
BusinessMeet_003=I was particularly struck by the fine, gray exterior with hip and gable roofing structures and metal spires. A proper gentleman of distinguished inclinations - and wealth to match - no doubt resided within.
BusinessMeet_004=The estate on the hill was clearly owned by an individual with similar tastes to my family. {_rnd_BusinessMeet_0}
BusinessMeet_005=Above the door, I noticed the nameplate engraved in stone: Count Vlad III Dracula. **I entered and gave my name to the butler:**

# passages/00147-BusMeetC.mws.yaml
BusMeetC_005={_rnd_BusMeetC_0} "Donate and let's forget this rehabilitation business. Remember, **you are not obligated to pay now**. We will arrange payment in your **waning years**, I'm sure."

# passages/00148-BusMeetB.mws.yaml
BusMeetB_001={_rnd_BusMeetB_0} "Donate and let's forget this rehabilitation business. Remember, **you are not obligated to pay now**. We will arrange payment in your **waning years**, I'm sure."

# passages/00149-BusMeetA.mws.yaml
BusMeetA_001={_rnd_BusMeetA_0} "Donate and let's forget this rehabilitation business. Remember, **you are not obligated to pay now**. We will arrange payment in your **waning years**, I'm sure."
BusMeetA_002="**For $2**, I will guarantee a lucrative investment in labor _(you will immediately gain the Ball & Chain Estate Upgrade)."_
BusMeetA_003="**For $3**, I will offer you the **deed to my home** for use at your leisure when this Asylum business has concluded."

# passages/00150-BusMeetD.mws.yaml
BusMeetD_001={_rnd_BusMeetD_0} "Donate and let's forget this rehabilitation business. Remember, **you are not obligated to pay now**. We will arrange payment in your **waning years**, I'm sure."

# passages/00151-BusMeetE.mws.yaml
BusMeetE_001={_rnd_BusMeetE_0} "Donate and let's forget this rehabilitation business. Remember, **you are not obligated to pay now**. We will arrange payment in your **waning years**, I'm sure."

# passages/00152-AsylumMeet.mws.yaml
AsylumMeet_001=Retrieval of Property
AsylumMeet_002=**{tempas}'s Journal -** 
AsylumMeet_003=I soon discovered my lost servant, clad in a leather device that restricted the movement of their arms, but otherwise enjoying a walk among the grounds.
AsylumMeet_004=The alienist on staff described symptoms of extreme paranoia and dementia that seemed to coincide with their employment at my estate. "The patient was suffering from minor delusions and frayed nerves," they stated pointedly before offering an intriguing choice.
AsylumMeet_005=We find that many of these issues are solved by releasing some of the pressure on the cortex by drilling a dime-size hole in the skull.
AsylumMeet_006=The cerebellum is especially sensitive to a concentrated electrical shock. While the singed skin and hair produce a noxious smell, the effectiveness is undeniable.
AsylumMeet_007="We can entrust them to your care again now. Or for a minor fee; complete the rehabilitative process. {_rnd_AsylumMeet_0} They become very placid."
AsylumMeet_008=Choose one of the options below:
AsylumMeet_009=**Pay $1 to gain a Caretaker from Lost.**
AsylumMeet_011=**Gain a Servant from Lost.**

# passages/00153-S4CompareTotals.mws.yaml
S4CompareTotals_001=Total Contributions
S4CompareTotals_002=The Asylum received a total of **${asylumcount}** in donations.
S4CompareTotals_003=The Count received a total of **${businesscount}** in donations.
S4CompareTotals_004=Hopefully this support will strengthen our relationship with the Asylum.
S4CompareTotals_005=The funds offered were equal. This indecisiveness will result in our perceived support for treatment.
S4CompareTotals_006=The Count will be pleased.

# passages/00154-BusThanks.mws.yaml
BusThanks_001=Thanks Are In Order
BusThanks_002=The old man stood abruptly and shook my hand. I felt an icy chill reverberate through my body.
BusThanks_003="Thank you for your contribution. 
BusThanks_004=But, if you'll indulge me, I have one more topic of conversation to address."
BusThanks_005=The old man then smiled in my direction and I saw the tips of his fangs extend over his ruby lips.
BusThanks_006=Now, if you'll excuse me, I am expected elsewhere and will have my man see you out. It has been a pleasure. An absolute delight."
BusThanks_007=I was offered a pastry and coffee on my way out, which I politely declined.
BusThanks_008=Immediately gain the **Ball & Chain** Estate Upgrade.
BusThanks_009=**Immediately gain {_rnd_BusThanks_0}VP.**

# passages/00155-BusNo.mws.yaml
BusNo_001=Declined Offer
BusNo_002=I'm afraid I must be obstinate in the nature of my offer.
BusNo_003=I'm terribly beside myself that we could not come to firm agreement.
BusNo_004=The man sniffed loudly, twitching his nostrils while his cheeks noticeably reddened. "Well I believe our business here is done. {_rnd_BusNo_0} I will have my man see you out. Goodbye, yes."
BusNo_005=I felt the door shutter close behind me abruptly as I exited. It took the entire carriage ride home to calm my nerves after that blustery event.

# passages/00156-BusBargain.mws.yaml
BusBargain_001=An Improved Deal
BusBargain_002=Well, it appears you have me at a disadvantage since I extended the invitation. How about I put in a good word with my charge at the Town Hall? I'm sure it would be nice to have some of your scientific achievements recognized by the public.
BusBargain_003=I was wise to contact you. You are unlike the other buffoons who would simply agree to any offer thrown at them. If I cannot tempt you with a monetary deal, perhaps my clout in academia will sway you. I will be sure to advertise your name to the universities in London upon my next visit.
BusBargain_004="Ahh, a shrewd negotiator," he stated with an air of incredulity, though I could not discern if it was a calculated effort to flatter me. "{_rnd_BusBargain_0}"
BusBargain_005=_If I decide to accept the offer, I will now receive a_ **few VPs** _along with my contribution._

# passages/00157-AsylumOpp2.mws.yaml
AsylumOpp2_001=Business Opportunity
AsylumOpp2_002=I have left out one singular detail of the event that gained my attention. As I was heading to my carriage, a tall old man with a long white mustache accosted me and noticed my disapproval of the situation. He was clad in black from head to foot with ruddy lips, frosted eyebrows, and a distinct paleness to his features.
AsylumOpp2_003="You don't believe this hogwash about rehabilitation, do you?" he asked while scrunching his aquiline nose. "French institutions and liberal nutcases all of them. Help them once and they'll **raise your taxes**, forcing you to help them again."
AsylumOpp2_004="Some people are made to be workers. And some unfortunate fools are born with insanities that cannot be cured. But, I believe that everyone has a place and every temperament a utility."
AsylumOpp2_005=The man invited me to stop by his newly acquired home on the outskirts of town, if perhaps I thought this Asylum could be better utilized for our mutual purposes.
AsylumOpp2_006=Place the **House on the Hill** tile on the main board near the Village Chronicle.
AsylumOpp2_007=Place a {icon:storybooktoken} **token** on that Location.

# passages/00158-Creature2.mws.yaml
Creature2_001=Turn to page 6 of the Village Chronicle.
Creature2_002=Turn to page 7 of the Village Chronicle.

