# passages/00174-JailEvent1.mws.yaml
JailEvent1_001=The Escape
JailEvent1_002=I met with their leader just days previous, through coercive means I assure you. There I was, forced to mingle with criminals and rust-covered sociopaths in coveralls, bruised and thrust upon the steps of the prison, or what they now call the Junk Palace.
JailEvent1_003=A woman stepped forward to the cheers of a throng of miscreants. Her hair was cropped shorter than a bob, dark and wild with a sheen of oil. It framed her angular face and draped over a black eye-patch that covered her left eye. She wore a thick apron that was once white, but now stained a dark crimson with fresh droplets of red bespattered across the chest. In her gloved hand, she held a metal cleaver, rusted near the handle, with thick divots in the blade from years of use.
JailEvent1_004=A man stepped forward to the cheers of a throng of miscreants. The man was strong and rough with a ruddy complexion, a broad, square jaw, and a beard separated by deep scars along his cheeks. He wore a thick apron with one shoulder strap ripped at the seams. The front was covered in dark stains, and by his confident stride, he seemed to revel in its uncleanliness. In his gloved hand, he held a hammer which dripped with a red substance that also stained his fingers.
JailEvent1_005="They call me {warden}. Perhaps you remember my family, and how they were ruined by the accusations of hysterical peons so many generations ago. Well now, us unfortunate wretches have taken back what is rightfully ours. {warden} runs this town."
JailEvent1_006=The aberrant horde roared their approval. The malcontented rabble beat their chests and clattered metal upon metal. 
JailEvent1_007=I spied a shadowy figure within the Junk Palace, its distorted silhouette framed against the entryway for a moment before disappearing once again. Was this the same creature I had hunted for?
JailEvent1_008="I have brought you here because you are useful. But mark my words, {warden} expects loyalty."

# passages/00175-JailEvent1A.mws.yaml
JailEvent1A_001=Build Me A Warrior
JailEvent1A_002=While I despised this cretin for their signature treatment of me, I also felt a strange sense of pride that my experiments had been appreciated, even by one so base. {warden} commanded an authority that I could not help but admire when the fear of immediate death had left me.
JailEvent1A_003="You will **build a warrior** to fight in the arena as will the rest of your kin. The winner will escape with their life. The rusted losers will be ground to dust for all to see on the floor of the Battledome. {warden} has spoken and so it will be done!"
JailEvent1A_004=Retrieve the cross-shaped **Battledome Warrior** tiles and give one to each player.
JailEvent1A_005=At the End of the Generation, each player will choose their single best Experiment of each type, place it face up in each of the 4 slots, and add its strength (VP total) to assemble their **Warrior** as noted on the Battledome Warrior tiles.

# passages/00176-ENTERTHEBATTLEDOME.mws.yaml
ENTERTHEBATTLEDOME_001=Enter the Battledome
ENTERTHEBATTLEDOME_002=The exterior of the iron dome was decorated extensively for the event, with sanguine cloths weaved into the archway at the front gate and a wild jumble of interconnected copper pipes sibilating with pressurized steam. With a loud whistle, the grand aluminium doors pistoned open, revealing the cracked earth of an ovular arena. All around myself and my cousins, the deranged citizens cheered in their strange attire and distorted physiques; begoggled and covered in an imposing mishmash of rusted metal and leather.
ENTERTHEBATTLEDOME_003={warden} sat on a copper throne at one end, its extensive base crafted from metal scraps.
ENTERTHEBATTLEDOME_004=My cousins and I had completed all other tasks. There was only this one final obligation. Before I left this world, I would cover this arena with blood and oil. The battle was on!

# passages/00177-LiberalIdeaInsert.mws.yaml
LiberalIdeaInsert_001=Last place gains points based on notes.
LiberalIdeaInsert_002=3VP per player ahead of you on the Score Track.

