AsylumTreatmentB_004=**Case Number: {_rnd_AsylumTreatmentB_0}-{_rnd_AsylumTreatmentB_1} -** _{question}._
AsylumTreatmentB_005=Subject shows mild psychotic tendencies, with dissociative behavior that is concerning.
AsylumTreatmentB_006=Subject exhibits compulsive behaviors associated with bouts of melancholy.
AsylumTreatmentB_007=Subject is obsessed with unfinished work.
AsylumTreatmentB_008=Subject appears to be suffering from grandiose delusions.
AsylumTreatmentB_009=Mild sedatives administered after an outburst of indignant anger brought on by receiving a 'poor' meal.
AsylumTreatmentB_010=Speaks obsessively about their legacy becoming tarnished by our intrusion into their affairs.
AsylumTreatmentB_011=Lashed out physically against another patient after they attempted to touch them.
AsylumTreatmentB_012=Along with manic episodes, this comorbidity of afflictions makes diagnosis a difficult task.
AsylumTreatmentB_013={_rnd_AsylumTreatmentB_2} {_rnd_AsylumTreatmentB_3}
AsylumTreatmentB_014=Repeated complaints about being misunderstood.
AsylumTreatmentB_015=Demands to be transferred to an asylum of actual repute.
AsylumTreatmentB_016=Idle threats to crush 'this infantile institution into dust' whilst emphasizing each word with a pounding of their fist.
AsylumTreatmentB_017=Initial evaluation inconclusive and will require further examination to determine the extent of disorders.
AsylumTreatmentB_018=Subdued and set to physical restraints after several attempts to flee the premises.
AsylumTreatmentB_019=Assessment remains ongoing. Possible mental instability.
AsylumTreatmentB_020=Patient's behavior is erratic, yet relatively harmless. Continued evaluation suggested
AsylumTreatmentB_021=Director 
AsylumTreatmentB_022=Vlad 
AsylumTreatmentB_023=intervened.
AsylumTreatmentB_024=Patient offered the opportunity for remote home care.
AsylumTreatmentB_025=**Choose an offer:**
