# passages/00185-StandardSign-inPageCode.mws.yaml
StandardSign_inPageCode_001=I gave my name to the butler
StandardSign_inPageCode_002=**Choose your player name:**

# passages/00187-NameEntryTown.mws.yaml
NameEntryTown_001=The Village
NameEntryTown_002=Now that our given names have been established, we must also search our recollection for the name of the village which our vast estates overlook. Considering the myriad of small towns in the Romanian countryside, it would be unmeritably forward to not allow the group a chance to collectively name the place they will now inhabit.
NameEntryTown_003=Click here to name the village...

# passages/00188-NameEntryTownConfirm.mws.yaml
NameEntryTownConfirm_001=Thank you and please do excuse our forgetfulness.
NameEntryTownConfirm_002=Of course, {townname} is an appropriate and fitting moniker for a place to conduct important scientific research. In fact, history will remember this name, mark my words.

# passages/00189-NoteSpecialBonusName.mws.yaml
NoteSpecialBonusName_001=Something special should be provided.

# passages/00190-RevengePlot35.mws.yaml
RevengePlot35_001=A Small Choice
RevengePlot35_002=**Carefully pick up this Storybook device and hand it to the player with the least VP.** _If there is a tie, hand this to the one who was last in turn order in the previous round._ **Do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
RevengePlot35_003=**Collected Notes -** _10 October, 1862._
RevengePlot35_004=Perhaps it was fate that understood my current misfortune and lackluster position compared to my cousins. But, a messenger arrived one day with an offer of punishment or deliverance that I alone would comprehend.
RevengePlot35_005=**MAKE A CHOICE:**
RevengePlot35_006=A {icon:storybooktoken} token will be placed on the **35VP** space of the VP Track. When the first player reaches this VP amount (including yourself), either fortune or misfortune will befall them.
RevengePlot35_007=Click here to choose Fortune
RevengePlot35_008= - The player will move forward one space for free on any Journal Track.
RevengePlot35_009=Click here to choose Misfortune
RevengePlot35_010= - The player will lose 3VP and send a Servant to Lost.

# passages/00191-RevengePlotFortune.mws.yaml
RevengePlotFortune_003=I, of course, chose **Fortune.** I was supremely confident in my abilities and in the utter ineptitude of my competition that I would claim this fortune before they would be able.

# passages/00192-RevengePlotMisfortune.mws.yaml
RevengePlotMisfortune_001=I, of course, chose **Misfortune.** Let this one act be the catalyst that dooms them to hell for their treacherous ways. May a thousand other miseries torment their souls. For I wish far greater ill upon them that hold me in such low regard!

# passages/00193-35Fortune.mws.yaml
_35Fortune_001=Fortunate Discovery
_35Fortune_004=A curious thing happened this morning. A courier arrived at my doorstep unannounced with a package. Upon opening it, I discovered a variety of notes and papers detailing unpublished scientific theories the likes of which caused my heart to quicken its pace. They appeared to be speckled with dried blood from an unknown source, but otherwise perfectly legible.
_35Fortune_005=No matter. What a marvelous boon!
_35Fortune_006=Immediately **move forward one space on any Journal Track** for no Knowledge cost. Then, return the {icon:storybooktoken} token to the supply.

# passages/00194-35Misfortune.mws.yaml
_35Misfortune_001=Misfortune
_35Misfortune_002=Today, I awoke to the unfortunate news that one of my servants had been burned alive while tending to the laundry. While certainly my recent laboratory security improvements may have been the culprit, the spontaneous combustion of human beings is still a rarity.
_35Misfortune_003=Suspect foul play. Will return to this after tea. Be sure to collect ashes.
_35Misfortune_004=Immediately **lose 3VP** and **return one of your Servants to Lost**. Then, return the {icon:storybooktoken} token to the supply.

# passages/00195-Creepy1stPlayer.mws.yaml
Creepy1stPlayer_001=Excellence Distrusted
Creepy1stPlayer_002=**Letter from** **{randomname} -** _November, 1892. Romania._
Creepy1stPlayer_003=It is deplorable in the highest degree for the people to distrust our presence because of the detestable business of our progenitors. {townname} is the place of my birth! Yet, here I write to you in haste with a fire to my diction. These cretins would penalize us for our very existence! They eye us with such apprehension that it preys upon my anxieties at every stretch.
Creepy1stPlayer_004=A pox on their wild superstitions! Oh, how I wish I were back in university!
Creepy1stPlayer_005=The player(s) with the most VP immediately **gains 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**

# passages/00196-Creepy1stPlayerB.mws.yaml
Creepy1stPlayerB_001=In Support of Others
Creepy1stPlayerB_002=**Letter from** _name illegible_ **-** _November, 1892. Romania._
Creepy1stPlayerB_003=The burden of fame has finally pressed its weight upon me. It is obvious from the awestruck silence upon my visits, that my cousins view me as an unrivaled inspiration and this sentiment has seeped into the mindset of the burghers as well.
Creepy1stPlayerB_004=While it vexes me to lose time to matters of local import, I cannot fault them for their inquiries. With the paranoiae of the past fading and my exemplary leadership on display, it is only natural. My affluence is my curse.
Creepy1stPlayerB_005=What a bother it is to be so popular.
Creepy1stPlayerB_006=The player(s) with the most VP immediately **loses 1** {icon:creepy_icon} and **discards 1 Experiment card** during the Start of a Generation phase.

# passages/00197-RehabNotes.mws.yaml
RehabNotes_001=Minor Consequence
RehabNotes_002=Bonus at start to level the playing field
RehabNotes_003=Obsession cards activate bonuses
RehabNotes_004=Treatment is successful
RehabNotes_005=Hunt vs BANK
RehabNotes_006=Asylum equals Creepy Track Treatment side game
RehabNotes_007=Liberal stuff
RehabNotes_008=Revive wife or more liberal stuff
RehabNotes_009=TOKEN: All Servants, including Spouse in Lost.
RehabNotes_010=Arent we choosing the PERFFEct Sanity number?
RehabNotes_011=Vampyre gives a Servant to each player.

# passages/00198-LowestJournalEvent.mws.yaml
LowestJournalEvent_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to the player who has advanced the fewest total steps in their Journal.** _(If there is a tie, the one who went later in turn order in the previous round breaks the tie.)_
LowestJournalEvent_002=That player gets to make a choice about a goal {icon:storybooktoken} token for the round.
LowestJournalEvent_003=Choose:
LowestJournalEvent_004=One choice.

# passages/00199-WhatifWampyre.mws.yaml
WhatifWampyre_001=Man sees the unfortunate wretches. It is most certainly unfair, but it is the way the world works. He is basically Count Dracula.
WhatifWampyre_002=For me it is so much easier.
WhatifWampyre_003=He desires faithful servants, but they are so, well, not expendable.
WhatifWampyre_004=The asylum is financially precarious. If they offer you an opportunity to invest, simply refuse and I will provide free labor for your troubles. Good help is difficult to find, yes?
WhatifWampyre_005=Businessman offers to invest in privatization of the Asylum. If he can get control of the system. Easily can double the occupancy. Cheap labor.
WhatifWampyre_006=This will result in a free Servant from Lost at the start of every round.
WhatifWampyre_007=Description of home and meeting.
WhatifWampyre_008="It is so difficult these days to procure good servants, am I correct? There was once a time where a man could provide lodging for one of the unfortunate wretches and he would be called a kind-hearted soul. Now there are far too many papers to sign."
WhatifWampyre_009="The Asylum is in a financially precarious position. If they offer you an opportunity to invest, simply refuse and I will provide free labor for your troubles."
WhatifWampyre_010=(locks in the player as "free labor" if they refuse.)
WhatifWampyre_011=**Draw a Compulsion card** _(do not move on the Sanity Track)_**.**
WhatifWampyre_012=Storybook token:
WhatifWampyre_013=Asks the player for assistance in secret. Cure the visiting Count of his affliction.
WhatifWampyre_014=Cure him
WhatifWampyre_015=I understand that this will take some time to procure, but waiting is not something to which I am unaccustomed. I will be here if you wish to talk of other business in the future.
WhatifWampyre_016=**Special Setup**
WhatifWampyre_017=Return the Storybook token to the supply.
WhatifWampyre_018=Cure him by gifting him a C-Level Occult Experiment at the End of the Generation.
WhatifWampyre_019=Would you like to offer a cure to the Count for his affliction?
WhatifWampyre_020=Yes. _(You will donate a completed C-Level Occult Experiment.)_
WhatifWampyre_021=No. _(You must choose this option if you do not have a completed C-Level Experiment.)_
WhatifWampyre_022=Cure Yes.
WhatifWampyre_023="Thank you for what you have brought me. Upon being confronted with the reality of the situation, I must confess that the thought fills me with both trepidation and comfort."
WhatifWampyre_024=Offers the BLESSING of STRIGOI. A Maladjustment card.
WhatifWampyre_025=2 Creepy at start. Your Self instead gains 3X the benefit of any Location in Town. Your Self instead can perform any Estate Action 2X with one placement.
WhatifWampyre_026=2 Creepy at start. $3 at start of the Generation.
WhatifWampyre_027=(Count does not appear in the next Generation.)
WhatifWampyre_028=Cure No.
WhatifWampyre_029="Perhaps it is for the best. "
WhatifWampyre_030=(Count appears in the next Generation.)
WhatifWampyre_031=Count Mad Max
WhatifWampyre_032=Appears at start to offer a free Servant to all.
WhatifWampyre_033=Is well aware and leaves an ominous warning.
WhatifWampyre_034="I caution you to not value their assistance too strongly. It is
WhatifWampyre_035=Count Asylum
WhatifWampyre_036=Becomes the head doctor of the Asylum. Appears youthful and full of energy.

# passages/00200-PrivateCountYesNo.mws.yaml
PrivateCountYesNo_001=Investment
PrivateCountYesNo_002=The Count returned this afternoon to make good on his promise of investment opportunities to our family. I noted how strange it was that my brief recollections of him as a child proved to be spot on. While my parents had passed, the Count seemed to have never aged a single day. The benefits of a healthy disposition and good living, I suppose.
PrivateCountYesNo_003=Each player **gains a Servant** from Lost.

# passages/00201-CreaturePleased.mws.yaml
CreaturePleased_002=An uncanny occurrence today: I was skimming through my family's notes and found references to an experiment to procure life from death. At this same moment, I received a letter with very poor penmanship from an individual signed only as **The Creature.**
CreaturePleased_003=The letter reads: "I wish to alleviate some of what ails you. Even from the cold of Siberia, where I reside away from the wretched eyes of humanity, I hear word of {townname} and its troubles.
CreaturePleased_004=I offer you this remuneration with no obligation. Your family may have cursed me, but it has also soothed the rage within me."
CreaturePleased_005=All players' remaining debts to **the Count** are removed.

# passages/00202-PlotPlayerCheckin.mws.yaml
PlotPlayerCheckin_001=The Mob Moves In
PlotPlayerCheckin_002=**Journal Entry -** _name and date illegible_
PlotPlayerCheckin_003=Another night of fitful sleep.
PlotPlayerCheckin_004=My unending spirit of invention, it once again leads the ignorant to my doorstep.
PlotPlayerCheckin_005=Last evening they congregated outside my gates, pitchforks and torches raised with aims to forcefully remove me from my own home. Had I not released the hounds to snap and gnaw at their efforts, their attempt may have been successful. Oh, why do they despise me so?
PlotPlayerCheckin_006=**Please choose the name of the overtaken player:**

# passages/00203-GainFamilyPlot.mws.yaml
GainFamilyPlot_001=A Separate Plot
GainFamilyPlot_002=**Letter from {tempplot} -** 
GainFamilyPlot_003=You have seen how they stare; how they accuse me without evidence or precedent. Well, I have tolerated their angry mobs and frontier justice for far too long!
GainFamilyPlot_004=I have planned for a grave plot to be installed upon the estate grounds to keep my remains from being contaminated in death by those who never accepted me in life. Yes, I take full responsibility for the rift this will cause between myself and the whole superstitious lot. Damn those insufferable peons!
GainFamilyPlot_005=I refuse to mend bridges built between myself and these simpletons. Why would I risk the inevitable defilement of our esteemed heritage in a public cemetery? My family will be buried upon my own lands by my own terms! I deserve to rest in peace while they deserve to rot in a hell of their own creation!
GainFamilyPlot_006=**At the End of the Generation, you will gain the Family Plot Upgrade.**

# passages/00204-HELPING.mws.yaml
HELPING_001=We should be helping the Asylum to improve their methods. It's only right!
HELPING_002=Submitting new and terrible treatments in a fun and competitive way. Pick a random discipline and ask for assistance.
HELPING_003=Engineering - Electrical Shock Physical Restraints
HELPING_004=Chemistry - Purgatives Sedatives
HELPING_005=Biology - Bloodletting Brain Repair Lobotomy
HELPING_006=Occult - Rest Cure Eugenics Exorcism
HELPING_007=Purgatives
HELPING_008=Bloodletting
HELPING_009=environment
HELPING_010=phrenological repair
HELPING_011=lobotomy
HELPING_012=physical restraints
HELPING_013=eugenics
HELPING_014=sedatives
HELPING_015=chloroform
HELPING_016=electricity
HELPING_017=rest cure
