# passages/00209-FOTU-End1.mws.yaml
FOTU_End1_001=Faded Into Obscurity
FOTU_End1_002=**Correspondence - {winner} -** _25 June, 1926_
FOTU_End1_003=It feels like ages since I have written. The village that we once sojourned to all those years ago has fallen silent. It's crumbling defenses are a reminder; a metaphor for the crippling isolation of xenophobia. Even now I remember those accursed city walls that sapped my youthful vitality with every visit into the murky depths of that place; a place that could never be rebuilt after the hideous Experiment was unleashed.
FOTU_End1_004=Yet, even now the indomitable pull of my family's infamous work tears at my very soul! No. I cannot carry on a legacy of fear that left an entire town and estate in ruins. My colleagues at the university have no reverence for me. They laugh so heartily when I tell them the town in which I was birthed. I do not blame them. My hope is that I shall never see that foul place again. How could my family cultivate such an embarrassing line of thinking?
FOTU_End1_005=As I pen this note, my lawyer has made arrangements for a transfer of ownership; the deed to that wretched estate will soon finally be wrested from my hands and with it, the insidious efforts contained within will be buried forever.

# passages/00210-FOTU-End2.mws.yaml
FOTU_End2_001=A Model City
FOTU_End2_002=**Journal Entry: {winner} -** _1 March, 1924._ 
FOTU_End2_003=I see now how wrong I had been. True inspiration, true science, true art, it emerges from isolation. Isolation is the catalyst. With silence and contemplation, the ability to truly focus without distractions, this is where perfection and enlightenment is achieved.
FOTU_End2_004=The citizens of {townname} were right in their decision. Outside influences only pollute the mind and distract.
FOTU_End2_005=One must be self-reliant and self-motivated. Science is instinctual. Brilliance doesn't come from universities. No one was ever remembered as the world's greatest team player. No.
FOTU_End2_006=The rest of the world may be unaware of my family's work, but that is all part of my ingenious plan. Today, I retreat to my laboratory. Soon, I will emerge from my scientific cocoon more brilliant than ever before and the world will tremble at my feet!

# passages/00211-IsoIdentificationSignIn.mws.yaml
IsoIdentificationSignIn_001=Citizenship Inspection
IsoIdentificationSignIn_002=**Journal Entry:** _name illegible -_ 
IsoIdentificationSignIn_003=Inspection day: Wore newest overcoat, but received no compliment from the reprobates attending the door. At least the security was lax enough that I was given no physical inspection upon entering the ramshackle government office.
IsoIdentificationSignIn_004=Dismal afternoon - overcast with a dreadful scud blanketing the town in grayness. When I arrived at the Town Hall for the scheduled inspection, I could only shake my head at the single individual in a recently re-stitched military uniform left-over from the 18th Century, sleeping at his post by the wooden double-doors. I decided to enter without rousing him to avoid investing any more time in my visit.
IsoIdentificationSignIn_005=**Please choose which player visited the Town Hall:**

# passages/00212-IsoIdentification.mws.yaml
IsoIdentification_001=Verification Completed
IsoIdentification_002=**Journal of {tempid} -** 
IsoIdentification_003=Shoddy. Regrettable. The Town Hall was all cobwebs and cracked plaster, with a set of ancient benches with black mold along the bases. The musty offices where I was to confirm my existence were in no better condition.
IsoIdentification_004=I received no cordial greeting. I received no additional bonus for my willingness to betray my own morals and submit to this oppressive occupation. I barely received the pleasantries of a greeting aside from a disinterested grunt from a sack-suited barrister loitering in the periphery. A clerk bid me sit with a handwave and it was an hour before the person handling my paperwork appeared.
IsoIdentification_005=Like a mangy hound, I was summarily dismissed and sent away after a brief glance at my papers and a lengthy interrogation. The officer in question was obviously less intent on law enforcement and more prone to surveying one's character with his eyes.
IsoIdentification_006=The interrogation was lengthy and lasted into the early evening. The individual in charge of my case had apparently been relishing the opportunity to 'nail me to the wall' as it were, and when my answers proved adequate and level-headed, the line of questioning became more aggressive. Did he think me a fool?
IsoIdentification_007=After an extended time, I was reluctantly approved. I bundled up my papers and my wits and beat a quick path to my hansom, where the horses stamped at my approach and appeared to be just as keen as I was to leave this wretched place.

# passages/00213-SmugEvent2ACont.mws.yaml
SmugEvent2ACont_001=Devastating and Expected Results
SmugEvent2ACont_002=**Journal of** **{randomname} -** _15 March, 1912._
SmugEvent2ACont_003=Experiment Notes - A Fabric That Cannot Become Stained: 
SmugEvent2ACont_004=While seemingly innocuous, our amazingly versatile fabric that could not be stained also appeared to have the more important side effect of repelling all possible stain sources with vicious force. Upon offering our fabric as a possible alternative for the town's flag, the light cloth explosively began to ascend and descend in mid-air, flapping wildly about the room. We fled City Hall and watched in mild amusement and terror as the experiment destroyed the building entirely within seconds.
SmugEvent2ACont_005=Experiment Notes - A Robot Servant That Prepares Meals with Lasers: 
SmugEvent2ACont_006=Possibly a flawed idea from the beginning and admittedly not our best overall craftsmanship, the robot butler almost immediately began to indscriminantly fire lasers literally everywhere. Our demonstration was very brief in City Hall, before we all retreated to a safer distance and observed the easily avoidable chaos that we had caused. The City Hall was engulfed in flames in minutes. Dreadful, really.
SmugEvent2ACont_007=Experiment Notes - Injecting an Agitated Gorilla with Hormones and Radium: 
SmugEvent2ACont_008=The cage in which our great primate was displayed was woefully inadequate, and upon the slightest provocation it emerged violently from its enclosure at the very beginning of our exhibition at City Hall. Covered in a disturbing amount of blood and viscera within seconds, the inevitable mistake rampaged through the room in a whirlwind of coffee and silver fur. We exited hastily to observe from a more appropriate distance as a hailstorm of shattered bones showered the nearby streets.
SmugEvent2ACont_009=However, undaunted, the Experiment continued its path of destruction until we were able to subdue it with our hastily prepared antidotal serum.

# passages/00214-PEWitch2.mws.yaml
PEWitch2_001=Progression
PEWitch2_002=Regression
PEWitch2_003=The relapse of paranoid delusion in the rural populace has made life particularly anxious for those who express a scientific aptitude. However, considering that the region's continued hysteria keeps most inhabitants locked within their ashen homes at night, fearful of every shadow that flits across the windowsill, I am reasonably sure that my new obsessions will blend into the macabre scenery unnoticed.
PEWitch2_004=I find with each passing evening that my parent's abhorrent obsessions boil beneath the surface of my everyday activities. Despite the village's push towards civility and the exploration of mental disabilities, I am unable to resist the clarion call of what could one day define our family's legacy! 
PEWitch2_005=**Retrieve the Obsession cards** _(18 total)_**.**

# passages/00215-PEWitch3.mws.yaml
PEWitch3_002=Exploration
PEWitch3_003=Agitation
PEWitch3_004=A Calmer Mindset
PEWitch3_005=An inclusive economy has reinvigorated the progressive ideals of the populace. Within years, this once guarded village has begun to embrace concepts of the future and to leave behind the ways of old.
PEWitch3_006=**If you completed your Obsession, draw a Maladjustment for this Generation.**
PEWitch3_007=The xenophobic tendencies of the population marry well with those of an extreme position. Those who display more conventional scientific aptitudes are looked upon with distrust.
PEWitch3_008=**If you** _did not_ **complete your Obsession, draw a Maladjustment for this Generation.**
PEWitch3_009=The push towards acceptance has allowed the citizens a meager respite from superstition. Some even look upon the advancements of science and technology as curious amusements.
PEWitch3_010=With the failure of government institutions causing a stressful atmosphere in the town, the people are again wary of the things that they cannot fully understand.

