# passages/00225-BattleIntro.mws.yaml
BattleIntro_001=The Main Event
BattleIntro_002=The announcer wheeled into the center of the iron ring on his penny-farthing and spoke into a rusted speaking-trumpet.
BattleIntro_003=**Presenting your combatants for this evening:**
BattleIntro_004={nameA}'s {_rpl_BattleIntro_0}.
BattleIntro_005={nameB}'s {_rpl_BattleIntro_1}.
BattleIntro_006={nameC}'s {_rpl_BattleIntro_2}.
BattleIntro_007={nameD}'s {_rpl_BattleIntro_3}.
BattleIntro_008={nameE}'s {_rpl_BattleIntro_4}.
BattleIntro_009=A sudden hiss of steam burst from the edges of the arena as my warrior took its place on the cracked earth alongside my cousin's. The sound of rusted metal clanging against the cage by the throngs of spectators heralded a stinging trumpet blast. With a final volley of flames, the battle had begun!

# passages/00227-BattleEnd.mws.yaml
BattleEnd_001=The Battle is Over
BattleEnd_002=**{nameA}**
BattleEnd_003=**{nameB}**
BattleEnd_004=**{nameC}**
BattleEnd_005=**{nameD}**
BattleEnd_006=**{nameE}**
BattleEnd_007=**'s Journal -** _February 11, 1923._
BattleEnd_008= emerged from the turbid pit of blood, oil, and iron to be crowned champion that day.
BattleEnd_009=I have struck the images from my mind, but the savage discipline {warden} afforded to each of my cousins for their failure was as swift as it was sanguinary. With heads literally severed from their households, I will be able to live out my final years in isolated study as the sole living member of this generation. I will relish this victory.
BattleEnd_010= gains **9VP**.

# passages/00228-TownHallExplanation.mws.yaml
TownHallExplanation_001=Town Hall
TownHallExplanation_002=When you visit the Town Hall, you may **pay $2 OR place a Servant into Lost** to gain a Memorial **Brick token** and **{brickvalue}VP**.
TownHallExplanation_003=_Bricks are placed into your Quarters. The Servant/Spouse piece discarded to Lost may be one you have already placed this round. However, it cannot be a piece placed below the {icon:insanity_icon} Track or already sacrificed to Perform an Experiment or Record Knowledge._
TownHallExplanation_004=The **Key to the City** Estate Upgrade will be awarded to the player who has collected the most bricks at the End of the Generation. 
TownHallExplanation_005=_If there is a tie, the one with the fewest VP will gain the Upgrade. If there is still a tie, the one who went last in turn order in the final round will gain the Upgrade._

# passages/00229-PEExplanation1.mws.yaml
PEExplanation1_001=Obsession!
PEExplanation1_002=Your **Obsession** card is kept face-up in front of you.
PEExplanation1_003=Next to a white diamond is a **new special ability** that you will perform each time you complete the action listed. This ability is in addition to any normal rewards you would receive.
PEExplanation1_004=**OBSESSION DEEPENS**
PEExplanation1_005=At the bottom of your Obsession is a task that you may complete and an amount of **VP** that is awarded if you do. When you complete your **Obsession Deepens** task, immediately gain the listed VP and flip the card face-down. _The Storybook will prompt you when to resolve any Obsessions that resolve at the END of a Generation._
PEExplanation1_006=Depending on whether you complete or do not complete your Obsession, you will be given a continuing Obsession in the next Generation _(more evil or more good)._ The path the story takes will also interact with your choice to complete or not complete your Obsession.

# passages/00230-ObsessionFAQ.mws.yaml
ObsessionFAQ_001=Common Obsession Clarifications
ObsessionFAQ_002=**White Diamond Abilities**
ObsessionFAQ_003=These are always optional. If you do not want to gain the benefit, you are not forced to gain the benefit.
ObsessionFAQ_004=**Obsession Deepens TIED/NO TIES**
ObsessionFAQ_005=If the ability lists NO TIES, you must have the most or least outright. If the ability lists OR TIED, as long as you share the most or least, you have completed the task.
ObsessionFAQ_006=**SPECIFIC CARDS**
ObsessionFAQ_007=**INFAMY**
ObsessionFAQ_008="You cannot visit Town Hall" with any of your pieces.
ObsessionFAQ_009=**RISING STAR**
ObsessionFAQ_010=The estate upgrade discount applies to the purchase price only, not for expanding to a new plot in your estate. If this ability would reduce the cost below $0, you do not receive ($) from the supply.

# passages/00231-PEExplanation2.mws.yaml
PEExplanation2_001=Obsession Penalty
PEExplanation2_002=Your Obsession card now lists a penalty.
PEExplanation2_003=Next to a **red** diamond is a **new penalty** rule that you **must** follow. If this penalty affects an action, the penalty is in addition to any normal rewards you would receive.

# passages/00232-BattleDomeExplanation.mws.yaml
BattleDomeExplanation_001=Battle Warrior
BattleDomeExplanation_002=The End of this Generation culminates in a scientific spectacle where {playtxt} mechanized combatants enter the dome and only one will exit.
BattleDomeExplanation_003=To form your Warrior, you will place your Battledome Warrior token in your play area and place any one completed Experiment of the matching type in each section. The **VP** amount listed on each Experiment determines the stat of your Warrior.
BattleDomeExplanation_004=Before the final battle, you will be asked to enter the stats of your Warrior. If you have no completed Experiments of a type, you will enter 0.
BattleDomeExplanation_005=The last Warrior remaining will receive **9VP**.

# passages/00233-PrivateRewardSignIn.mws.yaml
PrivateRewardSignIn_001=The Horror of Existence
PrivateRewardSignIn_002=**Journal Entry:** _name illegible_
PrivateRewardSignIn_003=I have indulged my darker side, pressed forward beyond my capacities and burned bridges with all my scientific colleagues. The day has come to meet with {warden}. I am ready to receive my hideous reward.

# passages/00234-JunkPalaceSignIn.mws.yaml
JunkPalaceSignIn_001=A Palace of Scraps
JunkPalaceSignIn_002=**Letter from** _name illegible_
JunkPalaceSignIn_003=Let me tell you of the day I ventured to the center of {townname} and met with {warden}. Though I will spare you the gory details of the horrors I witnessed upon my arrival.
JunkPalaceSignIn_004=The grounds of the old jail appeared even more imposing than they had been when the inmates were enclosed inside its iron walls. I made sure that my visit was brief, but with delinquent eyes upon me and obscene messages written on the walls in crude scarlet streaks, it was certainly not made short enough.
JunkPalaceSignIn_005=As I arrived at the steps of the Junk Palace, I was greeted by a rough guard wearing an apron fashioned with protective scraps of steel. 'Nice to meat you,' the man who introduced himself as 'Grinder' said. 'I have no beef with you.' And so I gained entrance to this decaying institution where the walls fall to pieces and metal springs from the Earth.

# passages/00235-JunkPalaceMeet1.mws.yaml
JunkPalaceMeet1_001=The Meeting at the Junk Palace
JunkPalaceMeet1_003={warden} stood up from the table where he had been enjoying a feast and crudely wiped his lips on his stained apron. He took me aside to speak privately. As privately as we could, being surrounded by three of his most loyal followers. They carried makeshift weapons with barbed wire wrapped around cudgeled ends and wore a similar thick apron to {warden}.
JunkPalaceMeet1_004={warden} stood and wiped her lips, and unceremoniously spit upon the floor. She bid me follow her to a portion of the jail where a large section of the second floor had collapsed and we could look out over the perverted land, its dismal cracks and ruddy mires stretching out for nearly a kilometer.
JunkPalaceMeet1_005={warden} spoke. "Since you have finally come down from your perch, I will reward you with an offer. For a minor sum, I will make sure your reputation around here is indisputable."
JunkPalaceMeet1_006=As you no doubt have realized from the dramatic retelling of this meeting that I have offered, I was skeptical of {warden}'s tone. "I assure you, I will spread knowledge of your experiments. All of Transylvania will fear you - at least, more than they already do. I want them to _hate_ you as I do."
JunkPalaceMeet1_007=I kindly declined the offer.
JunkPalaceMeet1_008=$1. (to gain 1 Creepy)
JunkPalaceMeet1_009=Pay $1. Gain 1 Creepy.
JunkPalaceMeet1_010=$2. (to gain 2 Creepy)
JunkPalaceMeet1_011=Pay $2. Gain 2 Creepy.
JunkPalaceMeet1_012=$3. (to gain 3 Creepy)
JunkPalaceMeet1_013=Pay $3. Gain 3 Creepy.

# passages/00236-JunkPalaceMeetb.mws.yaml
JunkPalaceMeetb_001=Resolution
JunkPalaceMeetb_002=I was anxious to leave this desolate place, so when the {warden} nodded towards the exit, I sprang quickly at the opportunity and left at a brisk pace.
JunkPalaceMeetb_003=As I walked, {warden} pointed to a large individual who remained concealed in the shadows. The Creature noticed our attention and disappeared from view. "Your family could not help that poor creature, so I have not and will not reveal to you what will befall if you do not impress me _(reach the end of the_ {icon:creepy_icon} _Track)_. But **if you do not reach the end, there will be a penalty**. It is best you do not find out what."
JunkPalaceMeetb_004={warden} honored their word and I received the encouragement I had chosen.

# passages/00237-JailEvent1b.mws.yaml
JailEvent1b_001=The World is Not the Same
JailEvent1b_002=And so it is now that I am tolerated while I am still useful. {warden} demands tribute from me, but this oppressive edict carries with it a freedom to explore all potential scientific avenues without the rigors of academia or the scrutiny of the public. With each visit to the town, I witness sights that stick with me like tar underneath the fingernails.
JailEvent1b_003=However, the moment my servants enter the town limits, they are harassed by the inhabitants and driven back to the estate for sanctuary. But my loyal caretaker's disposition and appearance meshes exceedingly well with the locals, allowing them to enjoy a new sense of freedom.
JailEvent1b_004=Perhaps over time this will change, but with the world turned upside down, I suspect some adaptation will be required.
JailEvent1b_005=**New Rules**
JailEvent1b_006=You cannot place Servants/Spouse in TOWN until you have **reached or exceeded the** {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker.
JailEvent1b_007=Caretaker pieces can be placed in TOWN.

# passages/00238-2PS4Kill2.mws.yaml
_2PS4Kill2_004=Players are bidding for the right to choose who is executed. **The player who wins the bid will:**
_2PS4Kill2_005=**Choose to kill the Butcher or the Blacksmith**.

# passages/00239-PEWitch3b.mws.yaml
PEWitch3b_001=If {fate1} completed their Obsession, they gain the **INFAMY** card.
PEWitch3b_002=If they **did not**, they gain the **RISING STAR** card.
PEWitch3b_003=If {fate2} completed their Obsession, they gain the **LIMITLESS KNOWLEDGE** card.
PEWitch3b_004=If they **did not**, they gain the **GRAND KNOWLEDGE** card.
PEWitch3b_005=If {fate3} completed their Obsession, they gain the **TRUE SCIENCE** card.
PEWitch3b_006=If they **did not**, they gain **THE TRUEST SCIENCE** card.
PEWitch3b_007=If {fate4} completed their Obsession, they gain the **UTTER REVENGE** card.
PEWitch3b_008=If they **did not**, they gain the **SWEET REVENGE** card.
PEWitch3b_009=If {fate5} completed their Obsession, they gain the **COMMANDING RESPECT** card.
PEWitch3b_010=If they **did not**, they gain the **DEMANDING RESPECT** card.
PEWitch3b_011=If {fate6} completed their Obsession, they gain the **WITHOUT RESTRICTION** card.
PEWitch3b_012=If they **did not**, they gain **THE WORLD MUST BURN** card.
PEWitch3b_013=Discard and return ALL other **Obsession** cards to the Scenario box.

# passages/00240-WallEvent1b.mws.yaml
WallEvent1b_002=Count up the number of players who placed $1 in their hand. If this number is **more** than the number of players who abstained, we chose **Strength**. Otherwise, _even if tied_, we chose **Acceptance**.
WallEvent1b_003=**Please click on the vote's outcome:**
WallEvent1b_004=We chose Strength.
WallEvent1b_005=We chose Acceptance.

# passages/00241-IsolationCaravanResolve.mws.yaml
IsolationCaravanResolve_001=Neglected by the Caravan

# passages/00242-TensionCaravanResolve.mws.yaml
TensionCaravanResolve_001=Neglected

# passages/00243-TensionSetting.mws.yaml
TensionSetting_001=Two Sides
TensionSetting_002=There is a bizarre aura about the town - as if each place of business were radiating with a unique primal energy. Any time I visit a location in {townname}, it is like I am rousing the spirits of a faction.
TensionSetting_003=I'm sure it is nothing, yet I feel compelled to jot it down in these pages. Unrelated note: I should have the caretaker check that the gate hinges are reinforced and the fencing spikes sharpened. The devil goes away when he finds the door shut against him.
TensionSetting_004=Retrieve the **Romani token** {icon:s2_romanitoken} and place it on space **1** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.
TensionSetting_005=Return the **Suspicion** Marker to the box. Place the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker on space **14** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.

# passages/00244-AsylumSignIn.mws.yaml
AsylumSignIn_001=Visit to the Sanatorium
AsylumSignIn_002=The meager facility appeared bleak and outdated from its exterior; less a haven for the mentally ill and more a glorified tavern. Yet upon entering, I found the halls clean and the separation between patient quarters and caregiver offices to be adequate.
AsylumSignIn_003=**I gave my name to the receptionist:**

# passages/00245-AsylumComplete.mws.yaml
AsylumComplete_001=Perhaps Stubborn, Perhaps Illiterate
AsylumComplete_002=**Collected Letters - {tempas} -** 
AsylumComplete_003=The most unusual thing happened to me the other day. I am almost embarrassed to state it.
AsylumComplete_004=I decided to visit the new Asylum in town to inspect the structure and determine its suitability for further research and investment. I had a startling sense of déjà vu upon entering the institution which was further exacerbated by the puzzled look of the receptionist when I gave my name at the door. I think she half expected me to turn myself in.
AsylumComplete_005=Suddenly it came back to me that I had already visited for the first time and apparently don't follow instructions very well. Appreciatively, I was given a small sedative before exiting the halls of the laughing academy once more.
AsylumComplete_006={tempas} loses **1VP** _and has wasted everyone's time._

# passages/00246-BusinessMeetb.mws.yaml
BusinessMeetb_001=A Sly Investment
BusinessMeetb_002=**Journal Entry of {busm} -** 
BusinessMeetb_003=The Count and what appeared to be several visitors sharing similar, friendly, yet distant demeanors urged me towards a sumptuous banquet table arranged as if my presence had been expected that very evening. I dined upon portions of creamed pheasant, black puddings, ostropel, and a healthy share of plum brandy. The food was so varied and rich that I was surprised that when the courses waned a hunger still remained with me.
BusinessMeetb_004=The Count's attendant ushered me into the study, where the gentleman relaxed in a daychair sipping from a glass full of deep red wine. He bid me sit and we talked for many minutes as I observed the mahogany shelves that lined the room, overloaded with books that appeared so new the spines had not been cracked.
BusinessMeetb_005=At length, the Count brought up the business at hand. "I enjoy tradition. Unlike the wiles of modern philosophies which sway in and out of vogue, I believe that investment should be based not solely on the kindness of one's heart and a vague promise, but on real trade. I gain some thing, you gain some thing."
BusinessMeetb_006=He ventured that he had an offer that would intrigue me.

# passages/00247-NoteonDracula.mws.yaml
NoteonDracula_001=The Count Gains a Foothold
NoteonDracula_002=The Count Vanishes
NoteonDracula_003=I have no use for such things. Here is your paltry sum returned before I remove myself.
NoteonDracula_004=I have money. I am not motivated by such things. I wanted allegiance and I have gained it.
NoteonDracula_005=SPLIT
NoteonDracula_006=BLOODSMITH
NoteonDracula_007=Becomes the Asylum Owner/Doctor
NoteonDracula_008=Happy until the 2nd round. The land and the people are tainted.
NoteonDracula_009=thanks to the {cureplayer}
NoteonDracula_010=penalty to the {cureplayer}
NoteonDracula_011=House
NoteonDracula_012={bhome} gains **The House on the Hill** tile and places it face-up near their Estate.
NoteonDracula_013=**The House on the Hill** is a Location that only {bhome} can visit, but otherwise follows all placement rules of a Town Location.

# passages/00248-S4Asylum2.mws.yaml
S4Asylum2_001=Asylum Support
S4Asylum2_002=For a generous donation, the Asylum will offer a new service to anyone in our family who may prove interested: The Asylum has decided upon a **{asylumup}** program for their premium contributors. Financial investment could help fund further positive advancements within the town, but would the investment be worth it?
S4Asylum2_003=**Asylum Share**
S4Asylum2_004=Anytime you visit the Asylum, you may **return a Servant to Lost to take a Perform Experiment** action in addition to the effect of the Location. _This Servant may be a Servant you have already placed this round._
S4Asylum2_005=**Asylum Labor Union**
S4Asylum2_006=Anytime you visit the Asylum, you **gain $2** in addition to the effect of the Location.
S4Asylum2_007=**Key to the Asylum**
S4Asylum2_008=Anytime you visit the Asylum, you may **pay $2 to gain a Caretaker from Lost** in addition to the effect of the Location.
S4Asylum2_009=**Option to Donate**
S4Asylum2_010=Each player, in turn order, now has the opportunity to purchase this Upgrade for **${asupg}** or decline. If purchased, the Upgrade is built immediately. _(You must still pay any costs to expand to a new plot if required.)_
S4Asylum2_011=Once all have chosen, click to accept button.

# passages/00251-PrivateCountCure.mws.yaml
PrivateCountCure_004=Ever since, I have felt reinvigorated; strong of heart and pure of will. I find myself in a more talkative mood, and when I speak, people listen more intently. My accent has become slightly more pronounced, and I struggle to pronounce my W's correctly.

# passages/00252-S4CountCure.mws.yaml
S4CountCure_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to {cureplayer} and do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
S4CountCure_002=**A Cursed Cure**
S4CountCure_003=**Journal of {cureplayer} -** 
S4CountCure_004=Strange, though expected occurrence today: The old man that I had once visited came to my doorstep. Though his dark garments were well-pressed, he walked with an unsteady step, seemingly enfeebled by his ailment.
S4CountCure_005=He was cordial, but desperate in his hope that I had procured the needed cure for his supernatural affliction.
S4CountCure_006=**Will you offer a cure to the Count for his affliction?**
S4CountCure_007= _(You will donate a completed C-Level Occult Experiment.)_
S4CountCure_008= _(You must choose this option if you do not have a completed C-Level Occult Experiment.)_

# passages/00253-CountCureQuestion.mws.yaml
CountCureQuestion_001=**To Remove A Curse**
CountCureQuestion_002=Before I returned to my carriage, the old count entreated me once again, this time with words soft-spoken: "My friend," he spoke, "I understand that this will take some time to procure, but waiting is not something to which I am unaccustomed. I am in dire need of assistance from your alternative expertise. I am a vampyre."
CountCureQuestion_003=How he knew of my secret workings and why he then revealed the nature of his affliction I cannot know, but where the discovery would send a normal person into shock, the revelation delighted me.
CountCureQuestion_004="I have lived too many years with this undying thirst for blood with which to sustain my youth. If you provide me a cure, I will offer you the same gift of strength and vitality that I myself have harbored all these years."
CountCureQuestion_005=Place the {icon:storybooktoken} **token** from this Location in your Quarters.
CountCureQuestion_006=At the End of this Generation, the Count will return. You may decide to cure him by gifting him a **C-Level Occult Experiment** at the End of the Generation.

# passages/00254-RareCreatureBonus.mws.yaml
RareCreatureBonus_001=Minor Compassion
RareCreatureBonus_002=The Creature was not unrelenting in its vengeance. For upon the next morning, I discovered a heap of torn pages, scraps kept bundled in twine yet perfectly legible after all these years. Though my cousins and I had endured an unbearable hardship, my contribution was not left unrewarded.
RareCreatureBonus_003=The player with a completed **Puppy** or **Bride** Experiment receives several torn pages from your grandfather's journal.
RareCreatureBonus_004=They **move one space forward on the Journal Track of their choice** at no cost.

# passages/00255-Expedition3.mws.yaml
Expedition3_001=The Expedition Uncovers...
Expedition3_002=If the number of Clue symbols {icon:s2_hunttokenbackred} collected is equal to **{_rnd_Expedition3_0}** or more, the Creature is found and the hunt is a success. Otherwise, the hunt is unsuccessful.
Expedition3_003=**Were you successful in finding the Creature?**

# passages/00256-LibCountBlessing.mws.yaml
LibCountBlessing_001=Ever since, I have felt reinvigorated; strong of heart and pure of will. I find myself in a more talkative mood and when I speak, people listen more intently. My accent has become slightly more pronounced and I struggle to pronounce my W's correctly.

# passages/00257-LiberalEventGood.mws.yaml
LiberalEventGood_001=Perhaps the world has some justice in it after all! A generous benefactor has intercepted our lobbying attempts and seen to it all debts were paid.
LiberalEventGood_002=All I received was a brief letter where the local bank owner explained his reasoning thusly: "I have made a name for myself in the only field that doesn't care how ugly or vicious I am: business."
LiberalEventGood_003=He signed his letter only as **The Creature**, but on a vivid egg-shell parchment bearing the bank's watermark. Who was this gentleman?
LiberalEventGood_004=Any player who offered money towards the bribe regains all money spent and **gains 1** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**

# passages/00258-LiberalEvent3.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent3_001=Aid to the Institute
LiberalEvent3_002=It was only natural for my contributions to the Asylum to extend beyond the monetary. You are no doubt tired of hearing me repeat it, but their methods are timid and only mildly effective.
LiberalEvent3_003=The Asylum's direction has always been tenuous. With prevailing opinions shifting towards eugenics and heredity as unconquerable factors, they have received criticism from all arenas. I am skeptical of this new movement - perhaps I am always skeptical - for are we so resigned to the fate that god or biology has assigned to us? Can we not exercise our individual will and nurture better habits? Should we all throw up our hands and laze upon our daybeds lamenting our Mendelian inheritance?
LiberalEvent3_004=I think it is high time for an innovative, aggressive new program to be introduced. I have scheduled a meeting with the Asylum's director. You do not need to wish me luck. I will be persuasive. A change is on the horizon.

# passages/00259-LiberalEvent3b.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent3b_002=Once all players are ready, reveal the amounts bid simultaneously.
LiberalEvent3b_003=Players are bidding for the opportunity to choose the direction of the Asylum's studies. **The player who wins the bid will:**
LiberalEvent3b_004=**Choose the scientific discipline** - The player who has completed the most Experiments of this type will receive a reward at the End of the Generation.
LiberalEvent3b_005=**Name the Program**.
LiberalEvent3b_006=Only the player who wins the election must pay their bid to the supply. The others return their money to their Estates.

# passages/00260-LiberalEvent3Res.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent3Res_001=Choose the Program Focus
LiberalEvent3Res_002=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to the player who WON the bid.**
LiberalEvent3Res_003=At the End of the Generation, the player who has completed the MOST Experiments of the type chosen will receive the **Menagerie** Estate Upgrade.
LiberalEvent3Res_004=**Please choose the Experiment type you would like the program to focus upon:**
LiberalEvent3Res_005=Engineering.
LiberalEvent3Res_007=Chemistry.
LiberalEvent3Res_009=Biology.
LiberalEvent3Res_011=Occult.
LiberalEvent3Res_012=Occult

# passages/00261-LiberalEvent3Resa.mws.yaml
LiberalEvent3Resa_001=Please enter the name of your new rehabilitation program:
LiberalEvent3Resa_002=**Newsprint - {newspaper} -** _27 February, 1902._
LiberalEvent3Resa_003=The Asylum has announced a radical change to their rehabilitative efforts, incorporating the most advanced alienist treatment regimen. 
LiberalEvent3Resa_004=While officials remain tight-lipped as to the details of the procedure, a bishop of the local diocese has been given residence to perform blessings to those whose will has been overcome by demons. Patients are isolated from stimulation, prescribed a "rest cure," and given a special restorative tonic of local roots and herbs.
LiberalEvent3Resa_005=A new wing of the facility displays the complex machinery utilized in this fascinating new therapy. Patients with varying degrees of dementia are carefully strapped to a hospital bed, while electrical pulses are concentrated upon different areas of the brain.
LiberalEvent3Resa_006=Using new advances in concentrated opiates, the doctors are able to administer strong sedatives to alleviate improper reflexes in patients. Through a combination of bloodletting and strong purgatives, the psychotic tendencies of the individual are allowed to exit the body.
LiberalEvent3Resa_007=An entirely rebuilt surgical stage has been constructed where visiting physicians and the public alike can view the procedures as they are perfected. By removing the offending portions of brain tissue, or by alleviating pressures in the skull, the mentally ill experience a transformative effect which renders them placid and focused.
LiberalEvent3Resa_008=While critics of the hospital remain outspoken, the progressive organization has embraced this change as proof that {townname} remains the most modern psychiatric refuge in all of Transylvania.
LiberalEvent3Resa_009=You gain **3VP**.
LiberalEvent3Resa_010=Retrieve the **Menagerie** Estate Upgrade
LiberalEvent3Resa_011=s.
LiberalEvent3Resa_012=At the End of the Generation, the player who has completed the most {mentype} experiments receives the **Menagerie** Upgrade. _Ties are broken by the one with the fewest VP._ 

# passages/00262-FOTU-End7.mws.yaml
FOTU_End7_001=Committed
FOTU_End7_002=**Case File: {winner} -** _July, 1926._
FOTU_End7_003=Patient exhibits no signs of previous paranoid delusions. Schizophrenic episodes have ceased though observation continues. Exercise regimen includes several unattended walks around the perimeter of the garden. Babbles repeatedly to themselves and others about "work left undone." Minor discomfort post-operation. 20 drops Tincture of Opium, dosed daily.
FOTU_End7_004=Demeanor: calm, distant. Not atypical for this type of rehabilitation.
FOTU_End7_005=Stitching area appears to have healed with no infection. Hair has begun to return around scarred area. Drill marks not noticeable.
FOTU_End7_006=Physician Assessment: Removal of frontal lobe considered a success. Maintain continued observation protocol. Reassess potential for home care after six months.

# passages/00263-FOTU-End8.mws.yaml
FOTU_End8_001=Taking Charge
FOTU_End8_002=**Letter from** 
FOTU_End8_003=**{winner}**
FOTU_End8_004=**Vlad III Dracula**
FOTU_End8_005= **-** _12 November, 1924._
FOTU_End8_006=It is my hope that this letter finds you well. The news I hear from Bucharest is positive, with a seasonable chill in the air and continued peace. As such, I pray you will indulge me in forgoing pleasantries and moving to matters of business with haste.
FOTU_End8_007=The institution in {townname} has been an unrivaled success. A steady stream of those suffering from insanities and delusions have been shipped here from other parts of the country. Yet still officials always wonder how we run such an efficient operation even as funding remains remarkably low. I believe it is in part due to the **{menname} Program** which has gained notoriety across Europe for its aggressive tactics. Those involved in the studies have shown a tremendous improvement in behavior.
FOTU_End8_008=Which is why I must repeat my strong request from my previous letter: we require more fresh patients to treat. Our near one hundred percent release rate has left several vacancies in the facility and we are in dire need to obtain more.
FOTU_End8_009=The concerns you expressed in your last letter are valid. What is the status of the released patients? How are we tracking their progress in society? How do you know we haven't simply been failing to treat them and then disposing of their bodies? Why are there bloodstains on the envelope of my previous letter? These are all important questions.
FOTU_End8_010=But, I ask you now; why question **results**?

# passages/00264-TaxesEventGood.mws.yaml
TaxesEventGood_001=Fortunately, as I arrived at the Town Hall to deliver my payment in person - yes, they impose a tax and then require me to courier it myself - a large gentleman in a well-tailored suit, wearing a large hat and a scarf about the bottom of his face stepped forward in my defense.
TaxesEventGood_002="No. No. I will take care of this misunderstanding," the man grumbled in a low and powerful voice. He produced a fountain pen from his breast pocket and with a flick of his wrist, my estate tax was excused in full.
TaxesEventGood_003="As the owner of the premier lending institution in {townname}, there are certain privileges I can indulge in for old friends," he stated confidentially. "Be sure to stop by some time and we can talk business."
TaxesEventGood_004=The creature winked, and his eye dangled from its socket with the motion. He quickly pressed it back into place with a gloved hand and made his exit before I could properly thank him. Who was that gentleman?
TaxesEventGood_005=Each player who chose to pay money to resolve their taxes recovers that amount back to their Quarters and **gains 2VP.**
TaxesEventGood_006=All other players **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00265-PaymentOrDeathA.mws.yaml
PaymentOrDeathA_005=They have just announced their intentions. The price has increased! They expect me to pay ${Acont} to them immediately or they will **KILL** me. Damn it all, I hear them pressing near!
PaymentOrDeathA_006=No, I would rather die. (You must choose this option if you cannot pay. Your Self will be returned to the box.)

# passages/00266-Payment2ThanksA.mws.yaml
Payment2ThanksA_002=**Journal Entry - {nameA} -** _1911._

# passages/00270-LiberalReplace.mws.yaml
LiberalReplace_001=Understanding and Support
LiberalReplace_002=**Letter from {randomname} -** _19 May, 1892. Romania._
LiberalReplace_003=The town's evolution has been a linear one towards relative peace, and this is in part due to the peace of mind that a mental health institute provides.
LiberalReplace_004=The Asylum has expanded not only their facilities, but their influence over the hearts and minds of the townsfolk. The former being not very difficult to do, I should say. However, it appears to be in good standing. 
LiberalReplace_005=I believe a Dr. Vlad Dracula has taken over as the head of the Asylum Program. I have heard positive things about him.
LiberalReplace_006=They have even embraced this idea of rehabilitation so fully that they are willing to send anyone for a general checkup when needed. I'm sure our phrenological colleagues might have a laugh at that one. But it is nice to know that the repercussions for pushing the envelope will be less severe.
LiberalReplace_007=Return the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker to box. Retrieve the **Rehabilitation token** {icon:s2_rehabilitationtoken} and place it one space to the left of the Suspicion Marker. _The Suspicion Marker remains on space {tracker}._
LiberalReplace_008=When your {icon:creepy_icon} Marker meets or exceeds the Rehabilitation token {icon:s2_rehabilitationtoken}, you will be admitted to the Asylum Program.

# passages/00271-Expedition2.mws.yaml
Expedition2_001=Expedition
Expedition2_002=Each player counts the number of Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront} they have acquired this round. The player(s) who has collected the most Hunt tokens {icon:s2_hunttokenfront} will set off on the expedition. _(All players tied for most set off on the expedition together.)_
Expedition2_003=The player(s) embarking on the expedition now flips their tokens to the reverse side and adds up the total number of Clues {icon:s2_hunttokenbackred} held by all players on the expedition.
Expedition2_004=Click to resolve the Hunt...

# passages/00272-JailEvent1c.mws.yaml
JailEvent1c_001=Merciful Heritage
JailEvent1c_002=A Sacrifice is Required
JailEvent1c_003=What will I do with this useless addition to my Estate now that the Asylum is no longer in operation? Surely a waste of energy to renovate such a specific extension. Better to dispose of it than to let it decay out of disuse.
JailEvent1c_004=All players return their {asylumup} tile to the Scenario box.
JailEvent1c_005={warden} has made one exception due to the previous generation and my **family's willingness to fund the Asylum**. They will continue to honor this pledge of service when we visit the Junk Palace.
JailEvent1c_006=**{asylumup} Rule**
JailEvent1c_007=When a player with the {asylumup} tile visits the Junk Palace, they may activate this ability.

# passages/00273-EndtotheCount.mws.yaml
EndtotheCount_001=An Abrupt End
EndtotheCount_002=**A Cryptic Letter -** _Count._
EndtotheCount_003=Due to recent events which have wrecked my investments and coated this village in a grimy filth, I find myself unable to procure fresh blood, as it were. With the region so tainted, I must renounce my involvement in the proceedings. I feel a deep regret at the suddenness of my departure, but my services are needed elsewhere.
EndtotheCount_004=Love and Sincere Thanks,
EndtotheCount_005=Vlad III
EndtotheCount_006=There is no bonus Servant this round. The Count has decided to no longer offer his services.
EndtotheCount_007=Each player ''gains 1 Resource'' of their choice as a parting gift. The Count has decided to no longer offer his services.

# passages/00274-PrivateInvestors.mws.yaml
PrivateInvestors_001=Investment Dividends
PrivateInvestors_002=Finances: Investments in {townname} by my parents have matured. I now own a substantial entrepreneurial stake in the village.
PrivateInvestors_003=I note this because I find it peculiar. Most of my family's investments are diversified amongst various trading interests in the Mediterranean, a very common theme even if I find it terribly dull. This new portfolio will directly increase my coffers; I pray it is the stimulus I need to advance my work more swiftly.
PrivateInvestors_004=Retrieve the Player {icon:s2_coloredmoneytoken} tokens from the Scenario box and give one to each player in their color. Starting with the player with the fewest VP and then to the next lowest, and so on, each player places their token on a Town Location of their choice. _If there is a tie, it is broken by turn order._
PrivateInvestors_005=When you visit a Location with a {icon:s2_coloredmoneytoken} token in another player's color, you must **pay $1** to the owner of that token.

# passages/00275-PrivatetoJail.mws.yaml
PrivatetoJail_001=Asylum Deteriorated
PrivatetoJail_002=I have just returned from a visit to the Asylum, or as they now refer to it, the {townname} Jail 
PrivatetoJail_003=under Count Vlad III Dracula's stewardship
PrivatetoJail_004=. Hastily built brick structures house hundreds of unfortunate wretches, deviants, and criminals alike, their mental afflictions varied and jumbled together. The grounds are in stark disrepair, and upon visitation, the noxious odors of unwashed and decaying flesh, human excrement, and drugged patients shackled to their bedding permeated throughout the complex.
PrivatetoJail_005=Needless to say, I feel little remorse in utilizing this ghastly place as a continued testing ground. Perhaps it would even improve the inmates' quality of life to know that their involuntary assistance will advance science forever.
PrivatetoJail_006=Turn to page **8** of the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00276-FOTU-End5.mws.yaml
FOTU_End5_001=Peace in Defiance
FOTU_End5_002=**Journal Entry - {winner} - 16 August, 1929**
FOTU_End5_003=Sunday: I had the glorious dream again - it never fails to reinvigorate me, as I could relive that moment each night for the remainder of my years and be content.
FOTU_End5_004=I watch with steady eyes as my family's creation, 
FOTU_End5_005=, with cathartic ambivalence, lifts the severed head of {warden} high into the air. I feel the searing heat of burning oil, hear the hiss of rising steam and smoke, and smell the rusted iron in the air. The crowded arena cheered even as their leader was torn from his makeshift throne and tossed lifeless to the dusty Earth, blood pooling beneath, dark and thick as motor oil.
FOTU_End5_006=These images appear in my mind like light on silver even as my weathered hands strain to grasp the quill. My last act of defiance, perhaps. But what is the worth of toppling a regional tyrant? All this effort to shake the world, and barely one square kilometer has been rattled.
FOTU_End5_007=The inmates have moved on. The town is an empty, ruined field without vegetation; a decaying pile of ash, rust, and mud. Some days my mind feels the same. The sense of peace does nothing to stem this emptiness of purpose inside of me. 
FOTU_End5_008=An old man visits now and then; a friend of the family with a withered face that he keeps wrapped tightly with a scarf.
FOTU_End5_009=What a waste contentment is! What a terrible investment! I only hope my progeny will leave this broken land behind and forge a new path.

# passages/00277-FOTU-End6.mws.yaml
FOTU_End6_001={warden} Forever
FOTU_End6_002=**Letter from {winner} - 5 May, 1925**
FOTU_End6_003=The customs of Transylvania are even stranger than I remember. I had vague recollections from my youth of being schooled in our home and shielded from the smoky village residing deep in that valley, but I could not have guessed the true reasoning behind it all.
FOTU_End6_004=I have forged an alliance with the local government based on my parent's good will. They have democratically elected {warden} and have even offered to provide materials and assistance for my continued experimentations. I would understand your initial apprehension at the moniker of {warden}, but I assure you that the title is derived from a regional dialect and is part of tradition. They have even fashioned a gaming arena of sorts within the town proper, where a particularly aggressive form of sparring is practiced.
FOTU_End6_005=In fact, I find this region to be surprisingly inclusive and accepting of the avant-garde, which suits my needs as you might expect. I have even scheduled a meeting this weekend with a local Count. He claims to have been a friend of the family and has resumed interest in business ventures within the district.

# passages/00278-FOTU-End3.mws.yaml
FOTU_End3_001=Springtime for {townname}
FOTU_End3_002=**Correspondence from {winner} -** _14 June, 1925_
FOTU_End3_003=If you can smell the scent of tea and rich pastries on this paper before you, it is because I write this letter to you from one of my favorite shops along the main street. The shuffling footsteps and metal din of automobiles along concrete allows my thoughts to wander. I find it disagreeably bright in these parts nowadays, but at least they serve a damn fine cuppa. There are definite benefits to traveling merchants offering a steady supply of fine goods.
FOTU_End3_004=It appears we have emerged from the dismal environs of yesteryear into a full springtime bloom. My family may have made a few missteps, but it seems their kind-hearted souls (of which I was not aware) won the day and assuaged the fears of the populace. I will say that it is rather enjoyable to sketch out new scientific diagrams in broad daylight without scrutiny.
FOTU_End3_005=There are even some willing to volunteer their time towards my "eccentric hobbies" as they call them. Such insufferable fools. I will take pleasure in exploiting their ignorance. But, I will try to be sensible about it - it is unseasonable weather for painful howling.
FOTU_End3_006=Anyway, send my best wishes to your mother and do not tarry too long.
FOTU_End3_007=Yours Always,

# passages/00279-FOTU-End4.mws.yaml
FOTU_End4_001=The Anger of the Mob
FOTU_End4_002=**Letter from {winner} -** _4 January, 1924_
FOTU_End4_003=It finally happened. They destroyed it all. Mobs with actual torches and pitchforks, I tell you, knocked down my properly erected fencing and stormed the estate, destroying my parents' work. The curs had the audacity to arrive unannounced; had I not heard the hounds eviscerating several members of the crowd, I may not have escaped before being swallowed up by the flames.
FOTU_End4_004=The grounds still remain fallow and singed by ash, enveloping the plot in a vast, dreary grayness. My entreaties to the governor have been met with indifference and ridicule. It is clear that I will receive no financial remuneration for this riotous behavior. Am I to be forever punished for the sins of my father?
FOTU_End4_005=No matter! What do they know of loss? I have lost everything. My family's legacy is in tatters. They drive us away as if we are the outsiders, like foreign beggars.
FOTU_End4_006=This is not over. I will have vengeance. This paltry village will rue the day it crossed, {winner}, the Fourth!
FOTU_End4_007=Also, if you would be so kind as to furnish me a small loan, it would certainly expedite my ability to obtain said revenge.

# passages/00280-BankLibExplain.mws.yaml
BankLibExplain_001=Bank and Library
BankLibExplain_002=**Bank**
BankLibExplain_003=When you visit the Bank, **gain $2.** _This is a_ {icon:creepy_icon} _action and will result in moving one space right on the_ {icon:creepy_icon} _Track._
BankLibExplain_004=**Library**
BankLibExplain_005=When you visit the Library, gain **your choice of 1 Knowledge of a type** listed. 
BankLibExplain_006=_Due to the death of the Butcher, there is no Biology Knowledge available._
BankLibExplain_007=_Due to the death of the Blacksmith, there is no Engineering Knowledge available._

# passages/00281-IsoBricksRes.mws.yaml
IsoBricksRes_001=Reward for Investment
IsoBricksRes_002=I have an interesting tidbit for you, since I know your propensity for such things. Oddly enough, my parents invested in the construction of the wall - for reasons unknown to me but reasons nonetheless. This has alleviated some of the hostilities against me when entering the limits of that lunatic asylum they call a town.
IsoBricksRes_003=Confirm that the Suspicion Marker is on space _{tracker}_.
IsoBricksRes_004=Count all bricks collected by all players. For every 3 bricks collected, move the Suspicion Marker one space to the right.

# passages/00282-IsoVerify.mws.yaml
IsoVerify_001=Verification of Identity Required
IsoVerify_002={nameA} loses **4VP** and must discard an Estate Upgrade to the box.
IsoVerify_003={nameB} loses **4VP** and must discard an Estate Upgrade to the box.
IsoVerify_004={nameC} loses **4VP** and must discard an Estate Upgrade to the box.
IsoVerify_005={nameD} loses **4VP** and must discard an Estate Upgrade to the box.
IsoVerify_006={nameE} loses **4VP** and must discard an Estate Upgrade to the box.
IsoVerify_007=All other players have completed their required verification and no penalty is assessed.

# passages/00283-WallCheck.mws.yaml
WallCheck_001=Our Donations to Strength
WallCheck_002=It was clear our donations were intended to be used alternatively, yet the resulting Memorial to solemnly remind {townname} residents and visitors alike of the perils of xenophobia is certainly a sight to behold. My family's contributions, or lack thereof, were still noted by the town. A pointless exercise, I think.
WallCheck_003=**Brick Count**
WallCheck_004=Count up all Memorial bricks that have been collected by all players.
WallCheck_005= or more pieces have been purchased, 
WallCheck_006=If fewer bricks have been purchased, 

# passages/00284-Gen3Token2.mws.yaml
Gen3Token2_001=A Life Forsaken
Gen3Token2_003=There was no one there to greet me on that day. As seemed fitting, for this was not some achievement to be unlocked - it was a personal decision that had long tore at the fiber of my being.
Gen3Token2_004=Though the appointed time had come, I did not attend the event. In fact, I spent most of my day lost in thought. It was something I should have done a long time ago.
Gen3Token2_005=I had come to a crossroads - a self-reckoning where the distress of existence was laid bare before me. I could continue onward on my path towards my appointed Obsession or I could forge a new path, one galvanized by my own impulses - wild and unfettered. Whichever I chose, I knew then that I would need to see it through to the bitter end.
Gen3Token2_006=**I chose:**
Gen3Token2_007=To keep my Obsession.
Gen3Token2_008= _(This option will award you_ **4VP** _for completing your Obsession or cause you to lose_ **4VP** _for leaving it incomplete. You_ **must** _choose this option if your Obsession is already completed.)_
Gen3Token2_009=To claim a new path.
Gen3Token2_010= _(This option will award you_ **4 Compulsions**_. You will discard your Obsession.)_

# passages/00285-Gen3Token2a.mws.yaml
Gen3Token2a_001=Conviction
Gen3Token2a_002=No. I did not succumb to fear and self-doubt. My course has been clear from the very outset. THIS was what I had always desired.
Gen3Token2a_003=After that moment, I was even more dedicated to the task at hand than I had ever been. My dear friend, I greet each new day now with a ferocity unimaginable and I swear to you, this resolve shall never again falter!
Gen3Token2a_004=**At the End of the Generation, if you have Deepened your Obsession, you will gain 4VP. Otherwise, you will lose 4VP.**

# passages/00286-Gen3Token2b.mws.yaml
Gen3Token2b_001=Rejecting My Fate
Gen3Token2b_002=Yes. For too long I have been shackled to predestination due to a sense of duty. And for what? For an ancestry who set these horrible events in motion and doomed me to an existence on the fringes of society?
Gen3Token2b_003=I will allow my thoughts to spread like tendrils of ivy, gleaning every ounce of sunlight from the gloom that surrounds me.
Gen3Token2b_004=I will allow the seed of genius to germinate in whatever fertile soil I deem necessary.
Gen3Token2b_005=My mind is made up. {_rnd_Gen3Token2b_0} I will not be tethered to the past!
Gen3Token2b_006=Discard your **Obsession** card to the Scenario box.
Gen3Token2b_007=Draw **4 Compulsion** cards.

# passages/00287-Gen3Token2SignIn.mws.yaml
Gen3Token2SignIn_001=At a Crossroads
Gen3Token2SignIn_002=**Journal of** _name illegible -_ 
Gen3Token2SignIn_003=Only the whistle of the wind and the scent of azaleas.
Gen3Token2SignIn_004=Only a cold, gray stillness and low-hanging clouds against an oppressive sky.
Gen3Token2SignIn_005=I arrived at the designated location, where two roads diverged just outside the town limits. But, I found no one there. {_rnd_Gen3Token2SignIn_0}
Gen3Token2SignIn_006=**Please choose your name:**

# passages/00288-TenseBricksRes.mws.yaml
TenseBricksRes_001=Minor Reward for Investment
TenseBricksRes_002=The local government was still thankful for the support. Since our donations assisted in the groundbreaking of the memorial, they reluctantly offered to return the favor. It was, quite frankly, the least they could do.
TenseBricksRes_003=Bricks can now be used to expand to new plots in your Estate.
TenseBricksRes_004=When expanding to a new plot, each brick token you spend is worth $1.

# passages/00290-JailEventA.mws.yaml
JailEventA_001=Hostile Takeover
JailEventA_002=If this letter reaches you, I urge you to delay any potential visit to this cursed village indefinitely! The lunatics have taken over the Asylum, quite literally.
JailEventA_003=Chaos! Utter chaos is the only way to describe the ensuing rebellion which has driven out the residents of {townname} and left a distorted landscape tattered in its wake. The inmates, sickened by their squalid conditions and driven deeper into madness, have reclaimed this bucolic village and transformed it into their own rusted wasteland. Oh my reckless ambitions! I have doomed this land to an apocalyptic fate.
JailEventA_004=Even now, the rivers run red with blood and acid mine drainage. How wrong I was to assume this exploitative business would be the end of things! Am I cursed to forever suffer for my family's hubris?
JailEventA_005=Turn to page **9** in the Village Chronicle. Return all {icon:s2_coloredmoneytoken} **tokens** to the Scenario box.

# passages/00291-PrivateReward1.mws.yaml
PrivateReward1_001=Junkyard Scrap
PrivateReward1_002=**Journal Entry: {tempname} -** 
PrivateReward1_003="What a joy it is to see your soul laid bare," {warden} said to me while gazing out a nearby window in the broken mess hall. The iron grate on the opening had been torn from the concrete and left mangled and exposed to the elements. It cast a twisted shadow across the stone floor. "I see that you are a monster by nature. And one cannot be blamed for simply following one's natural impulses."
PrivateReward1_004=I was stunned by the insinuation, but as {warden} raised 
PrivateReward1_005=his hammer and pounded it into his open palm, I remained silent. He continued.
PrivateReward1_006=her cleaver into the air and pointed it in my direction, I kept my objection to myself. She continued.
PrivateReward1_007= "Your fate is sealed and you are not to be forgiven, but you will be rewarded for what I have seen. And I will remember."
PrivateReward1_008=It was then that I was offered a choice that I did not expect and pondered on my carriage ride home. This patronizing generosity vexed me, but the words echoed in my mind.
PrivateReward1_009=Had I truly become a monster? Or was {warden} correct? Had I always been?
PrivateReward1_010=Draw the top 2 Estate Upgrades from the stack.
PrivateReward1_011=Build 1 of them at no cost and place the other on the bottom of the stack. _You must still pay any costs to expand to a new plot on your Estate._

