# passages/00329-CureCountYes.mws.yaml
CureCountYes_001=Cure Confirmed
CureCountYes_003=The old Count smiled, assessing the schematics which I had prepared. His long fingernails carefully rolled the parchment and he wrapped it with a singular piece of twine. "This will do nicely."
CureCountYes_004="I have made many mistakes over the past centuries. And I have made many enemies because of this. I am sorry to have misrepresented myself." The count turned towards me then, his white fangs perched upon his red lips and his elevated black collar obscuring a portion of his face. "I intend to use the cure. Just not upon myself. I will offer the cure to all of my enemies whether they crave it or not. With this, I will make these fools pay! Their bones will turn to dust, and I, Vlad Dracula will rise once more!" The old Count tilted his head back and cackled deep in his chest.
CureCountYes_005=The Count's laughter was infectious; I could not help but join in myself.
CureCountYes_006=Gain **2VP.**
CureCountYes_007=Discard one completed C-Level Occult Experiment.

# passages/00330-CureCountNo.mws.yaml
CureCountNo_001=Cure Denied
CureCountNo_002=The old man suddenly became animated, doffing his feeble demeanor and hissing like a feral cat. With a dramatic flourish, he whirled his cloak about him, swiftly wrapping himself in a dark cocoon. With a sudden burst of fog, the old Count vanished as a black cat jumped onto the windowsill. The cat fled through the open window and out into the night.
CureCountNo_003=All that remained was a red rose once stuck to his lapel, now fallen to the ground where it withered and dried right before my eyes. Perhaps, I had been rash in my judgement.

# passages/00331-PrivateHomeTile.mws.yaml
PrivateHomeTile_002=**Letter from {bhome}-** 
PrivateHomeTile_003=Due to the arrival of a strange package that included only a brass key placed upon a ruby silk pillow, I have just discovered a peculiar investment that my parents made. It appears I own a second home within this region.

