# passages/00360-CountTestResults.mws.yaml
CountTestResults_002=Uggh. 
CountTestResults_003=Perhaps it is unprofessional to pen my disgust upon the page, but this patient is completely undesirable for admittance. Or might I say, unfit for our institute's psychological consumption. Still, it is imperative that I negotiate the matter with the to-be-released {question} as I find myself unsatiated by this meager assessment. I am sure a referral to our glorious facility will suffice. Perhaps they know of one who is afflicted by instability - perhaps one well-fed, with rosy cheeks, and warm blood flowing through their veins.
CountTestResults_004=The patient is perfectly physically and mentally fit. I find absolutely nothing wrong with such a fine specimen of completely normal human breedstock and am utterly confused as to why they were admitted! Such sharp teeth, such glorious pallor, such divine form; why I wish all patients were so adequately equipped.
CountTestResults_005=Alas, despite such a **healthy**candidate for mental reformation, I must admit that they are too instrumental in the region to be confined to such dismal environs. No, I must satiate myself, and the Asylum, with others who are afflicted _(and less important)_. Release has thereby been procured upon certain private matters being addressed. It is my hope that they will provide a suitable referral in their stead.
CountTestResults_006=**Lose 1VP.** Then, immediately place one of your Caretaker or Servant pieces into Lost. If this piece has already performed an action this round, **lose 2VP**.
CountTestResults_008=You suffer no penalty. _The count would never harm a thrall._ Then, return your {icon:creepy_icon} marker to the starting space.
CountTestResults_009=Immediately place one of your Caretaker or Servant pieces into Lost. If this piece has already performed an action this round, **lose 2VP**.

# passages/00361-AsylumInterviewBegin.mws.yaml
AsylumInterviewBegin_001=Psychological Assessment
AsylumInterviewBegin_002=An informal interview has been completed. In the interest of administering a balanced battery of tests, we have decided to submit the patient to a formal evaluation. This test has been developed
AsylumInterviewBegin_003=under the supervision of Director Vlad III
AsylumInterviewBegin_004= to act as a general, psychoanalytical assessment, to assess the overall mental facilities of the individual.
AsylumInterviewBegin_005=This test will determine if the patient can be discharged, and if this is not advisable, what therapy they should receive.

# passages/00362-AsylumQuestion1.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion1_001=**Do any of your close relatives have a history of blood diseases? - Anemia? Hemophilia? Blood taint from sexual indiscretion?**
AsylumQuestion1_002=All of the above.
AsylumQuestion1_003=Not that I am aware.
AsylumQuestion1_004=I prefer not to answer.

# passages/00363-AsylumQuestion2.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion2_001=**What is your worst fear?**
AsylumQuestion2_002=Failure.
AsylumQuestion2_003=People.
AsylumQuestion2_004=I have no fears.
AsylumQuestion2_005=Spiders.

# passages/00364-AsylumQuestion3.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion3_001=**Do you have pains that appear and disappear without a physical source?**
AsylumQuestion3_002=Life... is... pain.

# passages/00365-AsylumQuestion4.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion4_001=**Do you have difficulty relaying the brilliance of your own ideas to others?**
AsylumQuestion4_002=They are all imbeciles!
AsylumQuestion4_003=Occasionally.
AsylumQuestion4_004=No one would dare question my authority in these matters.

# passages/00366-AsylumQuestion5.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion5_001=**It is opening night for a new theatrical performance and you are the star. As the curtains open and the lights go up, you realize that you are completely nude. What is your reaction?**
AsylumQuestion5_002=The show must go on!
AsylumQuestion5_003=Shame or Embarassment.
AsylumQuestion5_004=I feel nothing.

# passages/00367-AsylumQuestion6.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion6_001=**Are you prone to bouts of sadness that make performing basic daily tasks difficult?**
AsylumQuestion6_002=I wouldn't call it 'sadness.' I would call it disgust... at the world.
AsylumQuestion6_003=My heart is forever heavy.
AsylumQuestion6_004=Very infrequently.
AsylumQuestion6_005=I am never sad.

# passages/00368-AsylumQuestion7.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion7_001=**You are preparing yourself for an upcoming engagement. At this engagement, you know that you will have to make a short speech. If this speech is successful, it could mean a promotion at your place of business. What is your temperament?** 
AsylumQuestion7_002=I am well-prepared and excited.
AsylumQuestion7_003=I am nervous or ill-prepared.
AsylumQuestion7_004=I feel nothing. Human beings are merely tools to an end.

# passages/00369-AsylumQuestion8.mws.yaml
AsylumQuestion8_001=**You are selected to receive an award for a recent achievement of yours - which has taken considerable effort on your part. A colleague congratulates you for your achievement and offers praise. How do you react to this praise?**
AsylumQuestion8_002=I would demand to see this praise in writing!
AsylumQuestion8_003=I silently accept it.
AsylumQuestion8_004=I do not easily accept praise.
AsylumQuestion8_005=Their praise is irrelevant.

